WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:10.240 align:start position:0%
You might think you know everything
there is to know about Henry VIII.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.840 align:start position:0%
You'll know he married six times
and had two of his [music] wives

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.840 align:start position:0%
executed.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:26.920 align:start position:0%
But the truth about our most famous king
is much [music] more complex

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.920 align:start position:0%
and far more compelling.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:34.760 align:start position:0%
This series tells Henry's story over six
of the most tumultuous decades in

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:42.160 align:start position:0%
English history,
separating the real man from the myth.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:47.000 align:start position:0%
To some, Henry was a cruel bully.
&gt;&gt; Henry was self-obsessed, desired

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:51.160 align:start position:0%
admiration. He could never be wrong.
&gt;&gt; He wanted the theater of punishment to

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:55.020 align:start position:0%
be perfect. This is what happens when
you defy Henry.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:01:00.600 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; To others, he was a charismatic and
[music] successful ruler.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:06.000 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He jousts, he rides, he sings. What more
could you want from this perfect prince?

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:10.960 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But Henry's personality, his innermost
thoughts [music] and his motivations

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:13.680 align:start position:0%
have remained elusive.
&gt;&gt; Today, we might call Henry a little bit

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:19.120 align:start position:0%
[music] OCD.
&gt;&gt; It was said of me couldn't hold

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:24.200 align:start position:0%
somebody's gaze. He felt uncomfortable.
&gt;&gt; Now, a team of Tudor experts have come

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:28.240 align:start position:0%
together to investigate who the real
Henry [music] was.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:31.520 align:start position:0%
They'll unearth never-before-seen
documents,

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:35.520 align:start position:0%
including some from the Vatican's
archives.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:41.160 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Thank you so much for showing me one of
the greatest prizes in Tudor history.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:48.360 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; And they'll go backstage at Henry's
court to unravel a murky world of power,

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:52.520 align:start position:0%
plots, and petrifying ambition.
&gt;&gt; The Tudor court is a bear pit. It's an

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:55.936 align:start position:0%
aggressive and violent place.
&gt;&gt; When somebody is no longer useful to

00:01:54.320 --> 00:02:01.052 align:start position:0%
him, that's it, he cuts them out.
[music] It's almost pathological.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:08.052 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He was willing to change the entire
country, even the entire map of Europe

00:02:03.732 --> 00:02:08.052 align:start position:0%
in order to get what he wanted.

00:02:14.172 --> 00:02:20.132 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry VIII is born on the 28th of June,
1491.

00:02:20.652 --> 00:02:26.052 align:start position:0%
But he's never meant to be [music] king
in the first place.

00:02:23.772 --> 00:02:30.812 align:start position:0%
He's the spare heir, living in the
shadow of his older brother, Prince

00:02:28.452 --> 00:02:35.852 align:start position:0%
Arthur.
&gt;&gt; As the second son, the younger of the

00:02:33.092 --> 00:02:40.332 align:start position:0%
princes, comparisons could be made with
Prince Harry. In fact, Henry was known

00:02:38.172 --> 00:02:43.692 align:start position:0%
as Harry for much of his childhood, and
there are some similarities physically

00:02:42.572 --> 00:02:48.492 align:start position:0%
as well.
He was allowed really to be a little bit

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:53.412 align:start position:0%
wilder, to indulge his favorite
pastimes. He just didn't have the same

00:02:50.892 --> 00:02:58.012 align:start position:0%
pressures as his elder brother.
&gt;&gt; Henry clearly sees himself as the spare

00:02:55.652 --> 00:03:01.972 align:start position:0%
rather than the uh I suppose in some
ways that might be liberating, but in

00:02:59.772 --> 00:03:06.412 align:start position:0%
other ways it might nurture a certain
jealousy. Henry later in life has this

00:03:04.452 --> 00:03:09.732 align:start position:0%
urge to prove himself all the time, to
show that he he can be a success even at

00:03:08.372 --> 00:03:12.332 align:start position:0%
his most successful, and there's
something that must relate that to his

00:03:11.572 --> 00:03:17.132 align:start position:0%
childhood.
&gt;&gt; His mother and all her female attendants

00:03:15.452 --> 00:03:22.292 align:start position:0%
spoiled him
and made sure that the hard knocks and

00:03:19.252 --> 00:03:27.332 align:start position:0%
bruises of boyhood weren't inflicted on
their charge. And anything he wanted, he

00:03:24.812 --> 00:03:27.332 align:start position:0%
got.

00:03:30.332 --> 00:03:36.932 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; As the second [music] son, Henry is
ignored by his father,

00:03:34.332 --> 00:03:42.172 align:start position:0%
and instead raised by his loving mother
in the protective female world of Eltham

00:03:39.572 --> 00:03:42.172 align:start position:0%
Palace.

00:03:43.172 --> 00:03:48.652 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's relationship with his mother was
unusually close.

00:03:49.452 --> 00:03:56.252 align:start position:0%
His mother seems to have taken a real
care for the education of her son. For a

00:03:54.532 --> 00:04:00.892 align:start position:0%
royal princess to grow up in this sort
of environment wasn't that unusual. For

00:03:58.492 --> 00:04:04.814 align:start position:0%
a royal prince, however, it was a little
bit strange, and it just goes to show

00:04:02.654 --> 00:04:11.174 align:start position:0%
how unimportant really Henry was
considered in the line of succession.

00:04:08.494 --> 00:04:15.934 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But when Henry is just 10 years old,
something happens that transforms his

00:04:13.494 --> 00:04:15.934 align:start position:0%
life.

00:04:16.254 --> 00:04:24.094 align:start position:0%
Unexpectedly,
his older brother dies,

00:04:20.174 --> 00:04:27.494 align:start position:0%
leaving him as heir to the throne.
&gt;&gt; He's no longer the second son, he's the

00:04:25.574 --> 00:04:31.974 align:start position:0%
first son, and he's going to be king of
England. It's hard for us to imagine the

00:04:29.454 --> 00:04:35.374 align:start position:0%
pressure on him. The idea of having to
take up that position.

00:04:36.214 --> 00:04:44.734 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; To make matters worse, Henry's beloved
mother, Elizabeth of York, dies just

00:04:41.653 --> 00:04:44.734 align:start position:0%
[music] months later.

00:04:47.214 --> 00:04:54.094 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Recently, this remarkable survival from
Henry's childhood has been revealed to

00:04:52.414 --> 00:04:57.854 align:start position:0%
us, and it's incredibly exciting.
Because for a long time, it was thought

00:04:56.094 --> 00:05:02.614 align:start position:0%
that this was just any old page in an
illuminated manuscript. But when we look

00:05:00.534 --> 00:05:07.774 align:start position:0%
behind this figure of King Henry the VII
here, we see King Henry the VIII as he

00:05:04.894 --> 00:05:12.254 align:start position:0%
later became as just a boy.
This weeping child on the edge of

00:05:10.473 --> 00:05:17.174 align:start position:0%
[music] an empty bed, that of his
mother. He can't contain his emotion.

00:05:15.174 --> 00:05:20.534 align:start position:0%
His head is thrown into his arms in
despair.

00:05:18.694 --> 00:05:26.054 align:start position:0%
We imagine Henry the VIII as being
someone that maybe didn't feel emotion,

00:05:23.014 --> 00:05:29.574 align:start position:0%
that wasn't affected by grief. But we
can see in his reaction to his mother's

00:05:27.854 --> 00:05:32.854 align:start position:0%
death that it really
broke his heart.

00:05:33.398 --> 00:05:38.174 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; He was now the heir to the throne, and

00:05:36.174 --> 00:05:41.454 align:start position:0%
he didn't have his mother to guide him.
He had instead a very different figure

00:05:40.014 --> 00:05:46.454 align:start position:0%
in his father,
uh a very problematic, I think, figure

00:05:44.494 --> 00:05:51.094 align:start position:0%
to try and move him into this new phase
of his life. And I don't think that made

00:05:48.094 --> 00:05:55.654 align:start position:0%
it any easier for him.
&gt;&gt; Henry's father, Henry the VII, won the

00:05:53.974 --> 00:06:01.214 align:start position:0%
Wars of the Roses,
a bitter civil war which lasted three

00:05:57.974 --> 00:06:08.935 align:start position:0%
decades and divided the kingdom.
As the first Tudor king, he united the

00:06:04.174 --> 00:06:08.935 align:start position:0%
warring houses of Lancaster and York.

00:06:08.975 --> 00:06:18.295 align:start position:0%
But he now reigns over an unstable and
uneasy peace.

00:06:13.935 --> 00:06:23.775 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Paranoia was part of the Tudor DNA. The
Tudors really had a rather tenuous,

00:06:21.015 --> 00:06:28.735 align:start position:0%
legally fragile claim to the throne of
England. They were a very insecure

00:06:27.375 --> 00:06:32.935 align:start position:0%
dynasty.
&gt;&gt; There is a seed of insecurity planted in

00:06:30.855 --> 00:06:36.455 align:start position:0%
Henry from a a very early age. The
political history of his father's reign

00:06:34.735 --> 00:06:40.655 align:start position:0%
has essentially been the history of
plots and conspiracies that hanging over

00:06:38.575 --> 00:06:44.415 align:start position:0%
from the Wars of the Roses. Who's in,
who's out, who's being watched.

00:06:50.295 --> 00:06:56.055 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Everything changes for Henry when he
becomes next in line to the throne.

00:06:56.095 --> 00:07:03.455 align:start position:0%
He is now brought up directly by his
controlling father.

00:06:59.695 --> 00:07:07.975 align:start position:0%
After years of being sidelined.
&gt;&gt; Henry's relationship with his father was

00:07:05.415 --> 00:07:12.095 align:start position:0%
really complex. There are lots of
eyewitness [music] accounts that Henry

00:07:09.655 --> 00:07:16.895 align:start position:0%
was never permitted to go out of the
palace. He was kept to his rooms and

00:07:14.415 --> 00:07:22.735 align:start position:0%
that when he did appear at court, he
never opened his mouth except to answer

00:07:19.575 --> 00:07:28.335 align:start position:0%
a question. This is so different to the
upbringing that Henry had known. He must

00:07:25.415 --> 00:07:32.895 align:start position:0%
have felt like a virtual prisoner.
As soon as Henry VIII is brought under

00:07:30.615 --> 00:07:38.135 align:start position:0%
his father's control, you see his
personality just being squished. Almost

00:07:35.535 --> 00:07:41.895 align:start position:0%
this overbearing weight of his father's
anxieties, his [music] paranoia, his

00:07:40.415 --> 00:07:46.255 align:start position:0%
concern that something might happen to
this last vestige of the Tudor dynasty.

00:07:47.695 --> 00:07:53.175 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; As a very young boy, he [music] hadn't
really had much of his father's

00:07:51.255 --> 00:07:57.215 align:start position:0%
attention at all. But then of course,
suddenly Henry had too much of his

00:07:55.775 --> 00:08:02.055 align:start position:0%
father's attention. He found it
suffocating because Henry VII was trying

00:08:00.015 --> 00:08:07.537 align:start position:0%
to make up for lost time and kind of
chisel this young, wild prince into a

00:08:05.575 --> 00:08:13.057 align:start position:0%
future king.
Sometimes they argued quite violently in

00:08:10.737 --> 00:08:18.417 align:start position:0%
front of the court. On one occasion, a
scandalized ambassador reported, "It

00:08:15.937 --> 00:08:22.657 align:start position:0%
looked this evening as if the king might
murder his son."

00:08:20.657 --> 00:08:27.217 align:start position:0%
Little wonder there was a deeply
personal resentment against his father.

00:08:29.217 --> 00:08:35.977 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; After 7 [music] years of living under
this harsh regime, Henry finally

00:08:33.617 --> 00:08:36.857 align:start position:0%
glimpses freedom. His father is now
dying,

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:40.897 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; and Henry has been summoned to see him

00:08:38.457 --> 00:08:46.377 align:start position:0%
one last time. He knows that in a few
short hours, his father will be [music]

00:08:42.817 --> 00:08:51.017 align:start position:0%
dead, and he will be king.
&gt;&gt; This is a king who's dying, still not

00:08:48.597 --> 00:08:55.297 align:start position:0%
[music] feeling anywhere near secure on
his throne. He wants the Tudor dynasty

00:08:52.817 --> 00:09:00.377 align:start position:0%
to continue. So, to his last breath,
he's giving advice to his son how to

00:08:57.777 --> 00:09:04.457 align:start position:0%
secure the realm, what sort of advisers
to surround himself with.

00:09:02.217 --> 00:09:09.217 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He told Henry that he had to marry
Catherine of Aragon, the widow of his

00:09:06.857 --> 00:09:14.697 align:start position:0%
elder brother Arthur, and he would rule
England with her. It wasn't a sort of if

00:09:11.897 --> 00:09:18.617 align:start position:0%
or but. This is what you're going to do.
And Henry meekly accepted it.

00:09:20.031 --> 00:09:22.051 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:09:27.497 --> 00:09:33.617 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; At exactly an hour before midnight,
Henry VII dies.

00:09:34.297 --> 00:09:41.577 align:start position:0%
In that moment, the 17-year-old Prince
Henry becomes King Henry VIII.

00:09:42.857 --> 00:09:49.817 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's feelings about becoming king
would have been a mixture of

00:09:47.537 --> 00:09:55.817 align:start position:0%
apprehension about what was going to
happen, would [music] he be able to

00:09:51.857 --> 00:10:02.417 align:start position:0%
smoothly take over the levers of power,
mixed with a wonderful sense of relief

00:09:59.977 --> 00:10:07.177 align:start position:0%
that he was going to be his own man, his
own master, and he could do things which

00:10:04.817 --> 00:10:09.777 align:start position:0%
he wanted to do instead of other people
telling him.

00:10:12.658 --> 00:10:20.818 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Remarkably, no one outside that room
will hear there's a new king on the

00:10:16.498 --> 00:10:25.418 align:start position:0%
throne for two whole days.
The story of what happened in that

00:10:22.298 --> 00:10:28.418 align:start position:0%
48-hour period has intrigued historians
for centuries.

00:10:35.938 --> 00:10:42.898 align:start position:0%
The next 48 hours will decide the fate
of the kingdom.

00:10:40.738 --> 00:10:47.858 align:start position:0%
As soon as the old king dies, his
closest courtiers start plotting.

00:10:46.298 --> 00:10:50.498 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; When Henry VII dies, it's essentially a
coup coup.

00:10:51.898 --> 00:10:57.578 align:start position:0%
His death is [music] kept in secret for
all the best part of two days while in

00:10:56.018 --> 00:11:01.058 align:start position:0%
the background they decide [music] how
to bring on this new regime with a

00:10:59.498 --> 00:11:02.898 align:start position:0%
splash.
&gt;&gt; Henry played a full part

00:11:02.867 --> 00:11:07.298 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; in this great cover-up of his father's

00:11:06.098 --> 00:11:12.618 align:start position:0%
death. Of course, he had a vested
interest in it because he wanted to

00:11:09.698 --> 00:11:16.978 align:start position:0%
secure the throne.
&gt;&gt; For Henry, this is his first real

00:11:14.578 --> 00:11:22.378 align:start position:0%
experience of the ruthless machinations
of Tudor politics.

00:11:20.018 --> 00:11:27.418 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The Tudor court is a bear pit.
It's an aggressive and violent place.

00:11:25.338 --> 00:11:31.098 align:start position:0%
Your best friend can become your enemy
and your enemy can become your best

00:11:28.938 --> 00:11:36.738 align:start position:0%
friend.
&gt;&gt; You need to be able [music] to plan and

00:11:33.658 --> 00:11:40.258 align:start position:0%
plot your way through this vacuum of
power.

00:11:38.298 --> 00:11:45.538 align:start position:0%
And in order to do that, you have to
make sure that nobody knows the king is

00:11:42.138 --> 00:11:49.738 align:start position:0%
dead. Nobody has time to stage their own
coup d'état.

00:11:47.978 --> 00:11:54.978 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He must have been affected [music] by
this atmosphere of intense fear and

00:11:52.658 --> 00:12:01.898 align:start position:0%
suspicion, not knowing who to trust,
being very, very aware that actually the

00:11:57.618 --> 00:12:01.898 align:start position:0%
Tudors were a fragile dynasty.

00:12:02.938 --> 00:12:09.698 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry is convinced that the biggest
threat to his new reign is a rebellion

00:12:07.538 --> 00:12:13.099 align:start position:0%
coordinated by two of his father's
powerful advisers,

00:12:11.498 --> 00:12:17.619 align:start position:0%
Richard Empson
and Edmund Dudley.

00:12:15.779 --> 00:12:22.379 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Empson and Dudley were the sort of slick
apparatchiks that Henry the VII brought

00:12:19.539 --> 00:12:26.699 align:start position:0%
in to enforce his will, and they
resorted to unsavory methods, rigging

00:12:25.019 --> 00:12:31.299 align:start position:0%
juries, accusing people of crimes they
hadn't committed. And probably everybody

00:12:29.059 --> 00:12:35.059 align:start position:0%
disliked them.
&gt;&gt; Early on the morning of the 24th of

00:12:32.979 --> 00:12:39.659 align:start position:0%
April, 1509,
after 48 hours in limbo,

00:12:37.619 --> 00:12:43.699 align:start position:0%
Henry the VIII is finally proclaimed
king.

00:12:41.619 --> 00:12:48.819 align:start position:0%
But at the same time, he issues orders
for the arrests of Empson and Dudley.

00:12:47.179 --> 00:12:51.899 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Empson and Dudley are scapegoats.
They're convenient. You get rid of them,

00:12:50.499 --> 00:12:54.659 align:start position:0%
you appear to distance yourself from
what has gone before. Politicians do

00:12:54.099 --> 00:12:59.099 align:start position:0%
this.
&gt;&gt; Dudley, open the door!

00:12:56.099 --> 00:12:59.099 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Open up! Dudley!

00:12:59.139 --> 00:13:04.619 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; I think people had underestimated Henry
before because they may have thought

00:13:02.819 --> 00:13:08.939 align:start position:0%
that he was merely a puppet, that his
father was controlling. But now, Henry

00:13:06.739 --> 00:13:11.979 align:start position:0%
makes it very, very clear he's the one
calling the shots.

00:13:13.259 --> 00:13:16.139 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; In the name of the king!
&gt;&gt; What's the meaning of this?

00:13:15.299 --> 00:13:19.379 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; You're coming with us.
&gt;&gt; Ugh!

00:13:16.859 --> 00:13:23.899 align:start position:0%
Get your hands off me!
&gt;&gt; The arrests win the new king instant

00:13:21.579 --> 00:13:28.739 align:start position:0%
support with his people.
But it's likely that Henry has no

00:13:25.699 --> 00:13:28.739 align:start position:0%
ulterior motive.

00:13:29.579 --> 00:13:35.579 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry the VIII continued to resent his
father for for quite some time. He had

00:13:33.419 --> 00:13:40.139 align:start position:0%
had uh lots of his own impulses
suppressed for years and years. And

00:13:38.379 --> 00:13:42.859 align:start position:0%
because Henry couldn't do anything about
it as long as his father was king,

00:13:41.379 --> 00:13:46.779 align:start position:0%
[music] when he was gone, well, there's
an opportunity with Empson and Dudley to

00:13:44.579 --> 00:13:51.419 align:start position:0%
play out his irritations, his
frustrations with his father.

00:13:48.779 --> 00:13:51.419 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Tell the steward!

00:13:54.459 --> 00:14:01.219 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; On the same day, Henry issues a
groundbreaking piece of legislation,

00:13:58.939 --> 00:14:05.659 align:start position:0%
a general pardon.
This extraordinary document [music]

00:14:03.099 --> 00:14:09.819 align:start position:0%
sees Henry explicitly criticize his
father's reign.

00:14:07.379 --> 00:14:14.099 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; What Henry is trying to do is to win
popularity, and quickly. So, as well as

00:14:12.459 --> 00:14:17.461 align:start position:0%
getting rid of his father's despised
ministers, [music]

00:14:14.899 --> 00:14:21.501 align:start position:0%
he issues a general pardon to all of
those who'd fallen foul of Henry VII's

00:14:19.941 --> 00:14:26.021 align:start position:0%
justice. So, of course, this makes him
incredibly popular. People love [music]

00:14:23.701 --> 00:14:32.381 align:start position:0%
him.
&gt;&gt; Now, that pardon is basically rubbishing

00:14:28.981 --> 00:14:37.741 align:start position:0%
Henry VII. This is an extraordinary
a move that you use your father's

00:14:34.581 --> 00:14:42.581 align:start position:0%
unpopularity to sell yourself to your
subjects. Henry's telling his subjects

00:14:40.741 --> 00:14:48.861 align:start position:0%
that he knew they had suffered
grievously through injustices imposed by

00:14:45.901 --> 00:14:54.941 align:start position:0%
his father, and he was happy to do all
he could to right those wrongs.

00:14:52.461 --> 00:14:58.581 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He wants to begin in a way that is going
to make a break [music] with the past

00:14:56.421 --> 00:15:02.341 align:start position:0%
cuz it's all about reputation. It's all
about this gleam in his eye that he's

00:15:00.421 --> 00:15:06.301 align:start position:0%
going to be a famous monarch, the best
king that ever reigned in English

00:15:03.781 --> 00:15:06.301 align:start position:0%
history.

00:15:09.901 --> 00:15:15.021 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry is determined [music]
to distinguish his father's reign from

00:15:12.941 --> 00:15:18.701 align:start position:0%
his own.
But that doesn't stop him honoring his

00:15:16.701 --> 00:15:22.501 align:start position:0%
father's dying wish
and marrying his brother's widow,

00:15:20.821 --> 00:15:26.701 align:start position:0%
Catherine of Aragon,
just 7 weeks after [music] he becomes

00:15:24.301 --> 00:15:31.461 align:start position:0%
king.
&gt;&gt; Catherine is the most desirable bride in

00:15:29.455 --> 00:15:36.701 align:start position:0%
[music] Europe, the daughter of
Ferdinand and Isabella of Spain, the

00:15:34.341 --> 00:15:41.141 align:start position:0%
most mighty empire in the world [music]
at the time.

00:15:38.261 --> 00:15:43.781 align:start position:0%
But I think Henry really did love
Catherine of Aragon.

00:15:42.101 --> 00:15:46.021 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He professes himself to be deeply in
love. [music] He's part of those early

00:15:44.821 --> 00:15:50.861 align:start position:0%
grand gestures, which, you know, he
thinks he can make. But of course, he's

00:15:48.221 --> 00:15:54.221 align:start position:0%
also got an eye on security. And this is
a monarchy, so it means dynastic

00:15:52.381 --> 00:15:59.861 align:start position:0%
security, so it means a son.
&gt;&gt; His attempt to produce a male heir was

00:15:56.501 --> 00:16:04.581 align:start position:0%
pragmatic. He did not intend that the
decades of conflict that had preceded

00:16:02.541 --> 00:16:10.541 align:start position:0%
his father's reign would continue into
his reign. And he felt that only a

00:16:06.661 --> 00:16:16.781 align:start position:0%
legitimized male heir could do it.
&gt;&gt; Henry's dream [music] of producing a

00:16:12.141 --> 00:16:16.781 align:start position:0%
male heir soon comes true.

00:16:16.941 --> 00:16:22.182 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; On New Year's Day, 1511, [music]
Henry does have a son. Catherine of

00:16:20.582 --> 00:16:28.622 align:start position:0%
Aragon gives birth.
&gt;&gt; Henry was beside himself with joy at

00:16:25.702 --> 00:16:33.582 align:start position:0%
having a son and heir. His hopes and
dreams had been realized.

00:16:34.262 --> 00:16:42.782 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But Henry's happiness is short-lived.
His newborn son dies at just 7 weeks

00:16:40.342 --> 00:16:42.782 align:start position:0%
old.

00:16:46.382 --> 00:16:52.462 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry doesn't seem to have responded
very much at all to the news of his

00:16:50.622 --> 00:16:56.022 align:start position:0%
son's death.
He does comfort Catherine, but there's

00:16:54.062 --> 00:17:00.502 align:start position:0%
no real sense from any of the chronicles
or ambassador reports of this time that

00:16:57.702 --> 00:17:06.182 align:start position:0%
he is actually grieving himself. He is
able to almost put a full stop on that

00:17:02.982 --> 00:17:11.462 align:start position:0%
child life and move on from it.
He has something intrinsic within him

00:17:08.182 --> 00:17:14.982 align:start position:0%
that he can just be cold, that he can
shut down emotion.

00:17:16.221 --> 00:17:21.222 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [bell and music]
&gt;&gt; Throughout their marriage, Henry and

00:17:19.142 --> 00:17:24.942 align:start position:0%
Catherine will lose a total of six
children.

00:17:22.662 --> 00:17:29.222 align:start position:0%
And Henry's anxieties about having a son
and heir will intensify as the years go

00:17:27.702 --> 00:17:33.542 align:start position:0%
on.
&gt;&gt; The big what if of Henry's reign is had

00:17:31.502 --> 00:17:37.902 align:start position:0%
that young Prince Henry who was born on
New Year's Day 1511, had he survived,

00:17:36.702 --> 00:17:40.902 align:start position:0%
everything would have been different.
Henry would have had

00:17:39.502 --> 00:17:44.502 align:start position:0%
that son and heir from the beginning of
the reign. He would have had dynastic

00:17:42.382 --> 00:17:48.262 align:start position:0%
security. Maybe he would have relaxed a
bit.

00:17:45.582 --> 00:17:54.142 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; When Henry lost his son, Henry Duke of
Cornwall, he was also losing the

00:17:50.102 --> 00:18:00.102 align:start position:0%
opportunity to pass on his crown to a
legitimized male heir. He must have

00:17:57.542 --> 00:18:05.662 align:start position:0%
wondered at that moment whether that
marriage

00:18:01.902 --> 00:18:05.662 align:start position:0%
could produce a male heir.

00:18:06.102 --> 00:18:12.022 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; After 5 years of marriage, Henry still
doesn't have a son.

00:18:10.302 --> 00:18:15.502 align:start position:0%
And his new dynasty is beginning to show
signs of vulnerability.

00:18:17.302 --> 00:18:23.583 align:start position:0%
To bolster his authority,
he enlists the talents of a cardinal

00:18:21.903 --> 00:18:26.263 align:start position:0%
who has rapidly risen through the ranks
at court.

00:18:26.663 --> 00:18:32.263 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Cardinal Wolsey is a political genius, a
little mastermind. [music]

00:18:30.383 --> 00:18:35.623 align:start position:0%
He's Henry's fixer.
And you know, he does an incredibly good

00:18:33.943 --> 00:18:39.983 align:start position:0%
job because Wolsey was the man who would
relieve him of all the tedious business

00:18:37.463 --> 00:18:44.103 align:start position:0%
of state. He's the guy who's going to
help Henry fulfill his desires. [music]

00:18:42.383 --> 00:18:46.783 align:start position:0%
If the king wants it, Wolsey will
deliver it.

00:18:47.383 --> 00:18:53.983 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Wolsey is a churchman, but let's just
say he's not the sort of vicar that

00:18:52.103 --> 00:18:58.703 align:start position:0%
you'd sit down to tea and biscuits with.
He likes the finer things in life. He

00:18:56.743 --> 00:19:04.343 align:start position:0%
insists on being served on golden
plates. He surrounds himself by luxury,

00:19:01.823 --> 00:19:09.103 align:start position:0%
and he also has a few mistresses. He has
at least one illegitimate child.

00:19:07.423 --> 00:19:13.783 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Thomas Wolsey is somebody who's come
from a relatively poor background. He's

00:19:11.823 --> 00:19:16.783 align:start position:0%
the son of a butcher, and people will
make jokes about this throughout his

00:19:15.543 --> 00:19:21.343 align:start position:0%
career.
He's risen up through the church to

00:19:18.423 --> 00:19:25.783 align:start position:0%
become somebody influential who wants to
make a difference, and who is delighted

00:19:24.103 --> 00:19:29.583 align:start position:0%
have the opportunity in government to
put all his ideas into practice.

00:19:34.863 --> 00:19:39.783 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; For Henry, Wolsey becomes indispensable.

00:19:40.743 --> 00:19:48.383 align:start position:0%
Henry has always loved outdoor pursuits.
And whilst he hunts, jousts, and fights,

00:19:46.303 --> 00:19:53.183 align:start position:0%
the cardinal takes all matters of state
into his own hands.

00:19:51.063 --> 00:19:59.023 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry in his 20s often described as the
most handsome prince in Europe. He was

00:19:55.703 --> 00:20:05.743 align:start position:0%
6'1, stood above the other courtiers,
and he certainly stood above the general

00:20:01.583 --> 00:20:05.743 align:start position:0%
populace. They could see him coming.

00:20:12.183 --> 00:20:17.658 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; One of the really important things about
Henry and Wolsey's relationship is that

00:20:16.023 --> 00:20:20.743 align:start position:0%
Henry really does believe that Wolsey is
[music] his friend.

00:20:18.943 --> 00:20:24.345 align:start position:0%
They walk about together arm-in-arm in
the king's privy garden.

00:20:22.663 --> 00:20:28.745 align:start position:0%
Wolsey can always walk in to see Henry.
He doesn't need to make an appointment.

00:20:26.025 --> 00:20:33.585 align:start position:0%
Other ministers can't do that.
&gt;&gt; Wolsey he sees a huge opportunity for

00:20:30.905 --> 00:20:38.265 align:start position:0%
himself here and he takes it. According
to most courtiers he has absolutely no

00:20:35.865 --> 00:20:42.425 align:start position:0%
right to be there. He's of lowly birth.
He's worked his way to the top which is

00:20:39.985 --> 00:20:48.105 align:start position:0%
highly unusual but Henry really doesn't
have that same snobbishness that the

00:20:44.705 --> 00:20:48.105 align:start position:0%
rest of his court have.

00:20:48.905 --> 00:20:57.145 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Within a few years Henry raises Wolsey
to become [music] his chief counselor

00:20:53.585 --> 00:20:57.145 align:start position:0%
and one of his closest friends.

00:20:58.105 --> 00:21:04.025 align:start position:0%
Hidden away in the [music] archives of
the Vatican Library in Rome

00:21:01.905 --> 00:21:07.305 align:start position:0%
is a remarkable account
written by a 16th century Italian

00:21:05.905 --> 00:21:12.265 align:start position:0%
diplomat
which reveals more about their

00:21:08.545 --> 00:21:12.265 align:start position:0%
relationship than anything else.

00:21:12.465 --> 00:21:17.465 align:start position:0%
The Vatican has never given permission
for it to be filmed before.

00:21:17.945 --> 00:21:25.705 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Well, thank you so much for showing me
this work. This is the first time though

00:21:22.665 --> 00:21:28.625 align:start position:0%
that I've seen the original so it's it's
an absolute privilege of this wonderful

00:21:27.985 --> 00:21:33.985 align:start position:0%
work.
&gt;&gt; It's called Anglica Historia.

00:21:31.385 --> 00:21:38.345 align:start position:0%
It is about the history of England.
And the king himself

00:21:36.385 --> 00:21:42.705 align:start position:0%
Henry VIII
Arrigo VIII

00:21:40.665 --> 00:21:45.465 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The wonderful thing is for a historian
is this this is an eyewitness account

00:21:44.865 --> 00:21:51.225 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Yes.
&gt;&gt; of Henry VIII and his court. One of the

00:21:48.785 --> 00:21:56.545 align:start position:0%
best bits of his account is his
description of Cardinal Thomas Wolsey so

00:21:53.865 --> 00:22:00.585 align:start position:0%
Henry VIII's right-hand man.
I mean my Italian isn't great by any

00:21:58.905 --> 00:22:05.345 align:start position:0%
means but I think in the page we have
open here it says what a good fun Wolsey

00:22:02.905 --> 00:22:11.385 align:start position:0%
was as well. He would sing and
&gt;&gt; It talk about him cantava, saltava, so

00:22:08.265 --> 00:22:18.265 align:start position:0%
smiled, giocava, he told jokes.
&gt;&gt; So he would entertain and tell jokes and

00:22:15.105 --> 00:22:22.825 align:start position:0%
you can see the appeal of Wolsey for
Henry I think from this account.

00:22:23.545 --> 00:22:31.226 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; At first glance the document paints a
picture of Wolsey as an entertaining

00:22:27.866 --> 00:22:31.226 align:start position:0%
member of Henry's [music] court.

00:22:31.546 --> 00:22:37.346 align:start position:0%
But, it's not what it first seems.
It reveals that Wolsey has been

00:22:35.386 --> 00:22:42.426 align:start position:0%
manipulating Henry from the moment they
met.

00:22:39.746 --> 00:22:48.706 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; This account is not at all flattering
about Cardinal Wolsey and the methods

00:22:45.946 --> 00:22:52.466 align:start position:0%
that he employed to manipulate his royal
master. He describes him as a witty

00:22:51.226 --> 00:22:57.906 align:start position:0%
fellow
uh who would cling to the royal side,

00:22:55.146 --> 00:23:00.986 align:start position:0%
strum the lute, dance, indulge in
pleasant conversation.

00:22:59.746 --> 00:23:04.746 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He's almost doing his business by
stealth. Henry doesn't realize all the

00:23:02.906 --> 00:23:10.826 align:start position:0%
things he's agreeing to.
And that by these methods he would

00:23:07.146 --> 00:23:16.626 align:start position:0%
inculcate, instill, and drum into
Henry's ears all of the messages that

00:23:13.306 --> 00:23:23.106 align:start position:0%
Wolsey wanted to get across. My favorite
extract comes when he kind of lures

00:23:19.626 --> 00:23:26.946 align:start position:0%
Henry in by showing him a pretty jewel
or a ring. It's almost like he's

00:23:24.946 --> 00:23:32.266 align:start position:0%
treating Henry like a child, tempting
him with sweets. And Henry then just

00:23:29.506 --> 00:23:35.346 align:start position:0%
agrees to whatever the cardinal asks of
him.

00:23:33.546 --> 00:23:40.186 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's weakness [music] for flattery
and manipulation allows Cardinal Wolsey

00:23:38.146 --> 00:23:43.946 align:start position:0%
to rise to the highest echelons [music]
of court.

00:23:41.626 --> 00:23:49.386 align:start position:0%
But, in a few short years Henry will
turn on his close friend and advisor

00:23:46.306 --> 00:23:49.386 align:start position:0%
with a vengeance.

00:24:00.986 --> 00:24:08.266 align:start position:0%
Henry VIII is worrying over the future
of the Tudor [music] dynasty.

00:24:06.066 --> 00:24:13.026 align:start position:0%
He still doesn't have a male heir and
he's surrounded by potential rivals to

00:24:10.466 --> 00:24:18.786 align:start position:0%
the throne.
&gt;&gt; All his nightmares,

00:24:15.306 --> 00:24:23.026 align:start position:0%
all his problems, haven't gone away.
They've just been, like good wine, lying

00:24:21.426 --> 00:24:25.706 align:start position:0%
there getting stronger and more
colorful.

00:24:27.466 --> 00:24:35.268 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; As Henry gets into his 30s, we see
little glimmers of paranoia to the

00:24:32.788 --> 00:24:38.148 align:start position:0%
extent that he has started to change his
personality.

00:24:39.028 --> 00:24:43.467 align:start position:0%
He started to mistrust people around
[music] him.

00:24:51.908 --> 00:24:59.187 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; As his paranoia [music] grows,
Henry increases the provisions for his

00:24:56.268 --> 00:25:05.268 align:start position:0%
personal security.
&gt;&gt; There is a quite extraordinary security

00:25:02.227 --> 00:25:10.388 align:start position:0%
service surrounding this king. His food
is tasted before he's able to eat it.

00:25:07.867 --> 00:25:14.227 align:start position:0%
There's this elaborate ritual in order
to put him to bed [music] each night

00:25:11.788 --> 00:25:19.547 align:start position:0%
where the covers are checked for any
knives in his bed.

00:25:16.908 --> 00:25:24.202 align:start position:0%
What effect that must have had on Henry
because for all his confidence and his

00:25:22.107 --> 00:25:30.827 align:start position:0%
sense of invincibility, he's made
[music] very aware on a daily basis that

00:25:26.867 --> 00:25:30.827 align:start position:0%
really he's incredibly vulnerable.

00:25:31.347 --> 00:25:35.827 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's suspicions
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:25:32.908 --> 00:25:38.707 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; extend to the servants who surround him
day and night.

00:25:39.067 --> 00:25:45.867 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The barber is one of the very few people
who are allowed close proximity to

00:25:43.867 --> 00:25:50.148 align:start position:0%
Henry.
&gt;&gt; To be the royal [music] barber means

00:25:47.467 --> 00:25:55.307 align:start position:0%
that you are holding a sharpened blade
next to the king of England's throat.

00:25:53.427 --> 00:26:01.227 align:start position:0%
If you make one mistake, [music] you
killed a king, you committed treason.

00:25:58.627 --> 00:26:05.668 align:start position:0%
And so therefore it's very clearly
specified how a barber should be

00:26:02.947 --> 00:26:09.347 align:start position:0%
behaving, even what company they can
keep.

00:26:06.827 --> 00:26:14.388 align:start position:0%
These increasing provisions come from
his paranoia and they also start to feed

00:26:11.587 --> 00:26:19.827 align:start position:0%
it because every single part of Henry's
life was underscored with this sense of

00:26:16.827 --> 00:26:22.587 align:start position:0%
unease and suspicion about the people
around him.

00:26:25.987 --> 00:26:32.589 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry fears an uprising from a rival
claimant to the throne.

00:26:30.827 --> 00:26:37.229 align:start position:0%
And he hears a rumor that the Duke of
Buckingham is secretly plotting against

00:26:34.909 --> 00:26:42.429 align:start position:0%
him.
&gt;&gt; The Duke of Buckingham was the highest

00:26:39.229 --> 00:26:47.829 align:start position:0%
ranking nobleman in England, and he had
royal blood and lots of it. Henry is

00:26:45.389 --> 00:26:53.349 align:start position:0%
particularly suspicious of Buckingham
because he doesn't make any secret of

00:26:51.318 --> 00:26:59.229 align:start position:0%
[music] his claim to the throne, nor of
his desire to be king.

00:26:56.389 --> 00:27:04.629 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's suspicions reach boiling point.
And he writes a letter to Cardinal

00:27:00.589 --> 00:27:08.509 align:start position:0%
Wolsey that seals Buckingham's fate.
Henry's letter survives to this day. And

00:27:06.949 --> 00:27:11.109 align:start position:0%
it's held here at the British [music]
Library.

00:27:11.269 --> 00:27:18.309 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; It's extremely exciting for me to see
this original letter by Henry. There are

00:27:15.989 --> 00:27:23.909 align:start position:0%
actually aren't many of them because as
Henry himself says here, he finds

00:27:20.309 --> 00:27:29.589 align:start position:0%
writing tedious and painful. He tends to
entrust that task to scribe. So, the

00:27:26.349 --> 00:27:37.069 align:start position:0%
fact this is in Henry's hand is hugely
significant. This letter was intended

00:27:32.509 --> 00:27:44.229 align:start position:0%
for Wolsey's eyes only. It's top secret.
So, Henry is instructing Wolsey to keep

00:27:41.229 --> 00:27:50.109 align:start position:0%
good watch on the Duke of Buckingham. He
effectively wants Wolsey to spy on

00:27:47.149 --> 00:27:56.709 align:start position:0%
Buckingham. He is Henry's prime target.
He's the one he is most afraid of.

00:27:53.869 --> 00:28:01.189 align:start position:0%
Wolsey soon uncovers a whole raft of
evidence that's enough to condemn them

00:27:59.229 --> 00:28:05.749 align:start position:0%
Buckingham for treason. He's plotting
rebellion. He's even stealing some of

00:28:04.029 --> 00:28:11.109 align:start position:0%
Henry's own servants
and placing them in his household. Also,

00:28:08.389 --> 00:28:17.309 align:start position:0%
the thing that rankles most with Henry
is that a monk has prophesied that

00:28:13.829 --> 00:28:22.229 align:start position:0%
Buckingham will be king. Well, for a man
as paranoid as Henry,

00:28:20.749 --> 00:28:24.869 align:start position:0%
that really is going to be the nail in
the coffin.

00:28:24.989 --> 00:28:31.589 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Wolsey's investigation produces enough
evidence for Buckingham to be found

00:28:28.829 --> 00:28:35.950 align:start position:0%
guilty of treason.
And he is beheaded by an inept axeman

00:28:34.270 --> 00:28:38.630 align:start position:0%
who takes three strokes to cut through
his neck.

00:28:38.910 --> 00:28:46.590 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's treatment of Buckingham is one
of the earliest and most vivid

00:28:43.830 --> 00:28:51.150 align:start position:0%
indications of his brutality.
This caused shockwaves across the

00:28:48.990 --> 00:28:57.390 align:start position:0%
kingdom. He wasn't going to suffer any
hint of treason even amongst the highest

00:28:54.270 --> 00:28:57.390 align:start position:0%
nobles of the realm.

00:28:58.830 --> 00:29:05.230 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Fearing further [music] plots against
him, Henry's attitude to his noblemen

00:29:03.230 --> 00:29:10.470 align:start position:0%
changes.
&gt;&gt; Henry starts to get rid of some of those

00:29:08.310 --> 00:29:14.765 align:start position:0%
older courtiers and counselors who had
surrounded him for a long time. He

00:29:13.030 --> 00:29:17.150 align:start position:0%
mistrusts some of the old nobility
[music]

00:29:15.350 --> 00:29:20.870 align:start position:0%
because the Duke of Buckingham has
demonstrated that maybe they can't be

00:29:19.310 --> 00:29:25.510 align:start position:0%
entirely trusted, that they will have
agendas of their own.

00:29:23.310 --> 00:29:29.990 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He replaces them with the promiscuous
young aristocrats he grew up with, men

00:29:28.190 --> 00:29:34.710 align:start position:0%
he trusts.
But with such a debauched entourage,

00:29:32.150 --> 00:29:39.110 align:start position:0%
Henry's palaces are transformed into
houses of pleasure.

00:29:37.310 --> 00:29:42.710 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry has got an illegitimate son by
this point. One of his friends

00:29:40.710 --> 00:29:48.790 align:start position:0%
effectively is pimping out prostitutes
in the local area. It's really a place

00:29:45.270 --> 00:29:54.070 align:start position:0%
where sexual license and immorality are
completely rife.

00:29:52.190 --> 00:29:59.110 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Even though Henry joins in with all the
fun, at heart he's actually quite

00:29:56.870 --> 00:30:03.390 align:start position:0%
prudish.
&gt;&gt; You can almost picture Henry the morning

00:30:01.230 --> 00:30:08.430 align:start position:0%
after walking through this scene of
devastation with food strewn everywhere.

00:30:06.750 --> 00:30:13.910 align:start position:0%
There were people just sleeping on the
floor wherever they could.

00:30:11.670 --> 00:30:18.190 align:start position:0%
Henry's a real contradictory character
in all of this. So, on the one hand,

00:30:15.110 --> 00:30:22.350 align:start position:0%
he's encouraging this quite wild party
atmosphere, but on the other, he's quite

00:30:20.790 --> 00:30:26.350 align:start position:0%
fastidious.
I think actually today we might call

00:30:23.950 --> 00:30:31.350 align:start position:0%
Henry a little bit OCD. For as much as
he liked to project himself as a party

00:30:28.430 --> 00:30:36.041 align:start position:0%
boy, actually he found it all deeply
unsettling.

00:30:34.021 --> 00:30:36.041 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:30:36.110 --> 00:30:42.672 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The best evidence of Henry's controlling
behavior is contained in a little-known

00:30:40.552 --> 00:30:45.512 align:start position:0%
court document called the Eltham
Ordinances.

00:30:46.552 --> 00:30:52.872 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The Eltham Ordinances [music] are
effectively a great long list of rules

00:30:50.392 --> 00:30:58.392 align:start position:0%
that were drawn up by Cardinal Wolsey on
Henry VIII's command to reform the royal

00:30:55.992 --> 00:31:02.632 align:start position:0%
household. But what's fascinating about
them is that they give us an insight

00:31:00.552 --> 00:31:06.752 align:start position:0%
into Henry's psyche.
One of the things that's really clear

00:31:03.952 --> 00:31:10.912 align:start position:0%
here is just how bossy Henry is. He
instructs here that the people in his

00:31:08.312 --> 00:31:14.512 align:start position:0%
privy chamber shall be loving together
and of good unity and accord. So, in

00:31:13.272 --> 00:31:19.392 align:start position:0%
other words, go about your work with a
smile. And perhaps more importantly,

00:31:17.312 --> 00:31:23.592 align:start position:0%
keeping secret all such things as shall
be done or said in the same privy

00:31:21.552 --> 00:31:28.112 align:start position:0%
chamber. I mean, this is basically a
gagging order. If you're working for the

00:31:25.752 --> 00:31:32.231 align:start position:0%
king, then don't speak about what you
see or hear in the privy chamber.

00:31:35.072 --> 00:31:41.952 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But for the Cardinal Wolsey, the Eltham
Ordinances serve another purpose

00:31:39.512 --> 00:31:46.552 align:start position:0%
entirely.
&gt;&gt; Wolsey had an ulterior motive. He wanted

00:31:44.672 --> 00:31:51.352 align:start position:0%
to control the people who were getting
close to the king. He wanted to ensure

00:31:49.072 --> 00:31:55.712 align:start position:0%
that other people couldn't bend his ear.
And as it says here, not intermeddle of

00:31:53.471 --> 00:31:58.632 align:start position:0%
causes or matters. In other words, the
people who are close to the king should

00:31:57.152 --> 00:32:02.392 align:start position:0%
not be talking politics and they
shouldn't be trying to move up in the

00:32:00.072 --> 00:32:06.632 align:start position:0%
world. So, this is really something of a
political coup at the same time as it is

00:32:04.872 --> 00:32:09.352 align:start position:0%
a book of rules for how the household
should behave.

00:32:11.392 --> 00:32:19.392 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The Eltham Ordinances help Wolsey to
become the most powerful man in England

00:32:15.952 --> 00:32:19.392 align:start position:0%
other than the king himself.

00:32:19.552 --> 00:32:25.872 align:start position:0%
But there are signs that Henry feels the
cardinal is getting too big for his

00:32:23.512 --> 00:32:30.032 align:start position:0%
boots.
&gt;&gt; Wolsey runs a court that is spectacular.

00:32:28.592 --> 00:32:33.992 align:start position:0%
You know, when he holds parties at
Hampton Court, there are hundreds of

00:32:32.272 --> 00:32:38.753 align:start position:0%
people there for dinner.
But it's also getting to a point of

00:32:35.952 --> 00:32:41.953 align:start position:0%
almost competing with Henry himself. And
that's a bit of a problem.

00:32:41.993 --> 00:32:47.753 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry starts to look more closely to
what people are doing for him, and that

00:32:45.673 --> 00:32:53.113 align:start position:0%
includes Wolsey.
He's contradicting Wolsey from time to

00:32:49.513 --> 00:32:57.153 align:start position:0%
time. They have the odd little clash.
We think that somehow Henry was some

00:32:55.633 --> 00:33:00.673 align:start position:0%
sort of mental defective who needed his
minister to tell him what to do. That's

00:32:58.553 --> 00:33:05.313 align:start position:0%
not the case. I mean, Henry was always
in charge, even when he was just leaving

00:33:02.553 --> 00:33:10.673 align:start position:0%
things to other people.
&gt;&gt; A real indication of Henry's growing

00:33:07.633 --> 00:33:15.993 align:start position:0%
unease with Wolsey's status comes over
the issue of Hampton Court.

00:33:13.753 --> 00:33:20.553 align:start position:0%
Wolsey knows that Henry's a bit jealous
of it. [music] And when he realizes that

00:33:18.113 --> 00:33:26.513 align:start position:0%
he's starting to lose Henry's favor, he
makes this very symbolic gesture of

00:33:23.153 --> 00:33:26.513 align:start position:0%
giving it to the king.

00:33:31.953 --> 00:33:37.353 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; As his relationship with Wolsey begins
to unravel, [music]

00:33:35.433 --> 00:33:40.473 align:start position:0%
Henry's marriage to Catherine of Aragon
is falling apart.

00:33:40.673 --> 00:33:45.633 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; One of the deep-seated [music] things in
Henry's character is that if something

00:33:44.193 --> 00:33:50.553 align:start position:0%
goes wrong, it is always somebody else's
fault. And so, Henry does start to blame

00:33:48.673 --> 00:33:54.313 align:start position:0%
Catherine. After the birth of the
Princess Mary, [music] their only child,

00:33:52.713 --> 00:33:57.993 align:start position:0%
there are no more living children. And
then, of course, Catherine is almost 6

00:33:56.153 --> 00:34:01.593 align:start position:0%
years older than he is, and she's going
to enter the menopause, and that worries

00:33:59.993 --> 00:34:05.713 align:start position:0%
him.
&gt;&gt; Throughout his reign, Henry has this

00:34:03.233 --> 00:34:09.593 align:start position:0%
problem, which [music] is that
he's king, he's meant to be in charge of

00:34:08.033 --> 00:34:14.073 align:start position:0%
everything, he's meant to be able to
decide his own fate, [music]

00:34:11.633 --> 00:34:18.633 align:start position:0%
and yet there are so many places in his
life where he then discovers he's not in

00:34:16.953 --> 00:34:21.353 align:start position:0%
control of things.
He's not in control of whether his wife

00:34:20.433 --> 00:34:25.193 align:start position:0%
has a son.
&gt;&gt; A queen is [music] there for one

00:34:23.113 --> 00:34:28.433 align:start position:0%
principal purpose, and that is to
produce sons. And Catherine's not doing

00:34:26.993 --> 00:34:32.393 align:start position:0%
that, and therefore, you know, Henry,
he's bound to he's bound to look

00:34:29.833 --> 00:34:32.393 align:start position:0%
elsewhere.

00:34:34.153 --> 00:34:42.634 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's attentions are turning to a
young woman at court, Anne Boleyn.

00:34:40.033 --> 00:34:47.794 align:start position:0%
He's had affairs before, but this time
things feel different.

00:34:45.234 --> 00:34:51.834 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Anne plays things slightly differently.
As soon as it becomes apparent that

00:34:49.794 --> 00:34:55.634 align:start position:0%
Henry is considering the validity of his
marriage to Catherine of Aragon, she

00:34:53.434 --> 00:34:59.914 align:start position:0%
starts positioning herself as the
potential future bride. And Henry is

00:34:57.834 --> 00:35:05.314 align:start position:0%
quite happy to go along with this. And
so they start on this attempt to get

00:35:03.434 --> 00:35:09.434 align:start position:0%
Henry's marriage to Catherine declared
invalid.

00:35:07.434 --> 00:35:13.994 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Desperate to end his marriage, Henry
starts searching for a way to divorce

00:35:11.354 --> 00:35:13.994 align:start position:0%
Catherine.

00:35:14.154 --> 00:35:21.634 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Once Henry's decided that he wants to
marry Anne Boleyn, he goes all guns

00:35:17.194 --> 00:35:21.634 align:start position:0%
blazing to research this himself.

00:35:22.154 --> 00:35:29.274 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He gets it into his head that the reason
he has no sons is [music] because he has

00:35:27.234 --> 00:35:34.234 align:start position:0%
transgressed that biblical rule in
Leviticus that you must not marry your

00:35:31.314 --> 00:35:34.234 align:start position:0%
brother's widow.

00:35:34.474 --> 00:35:40.674 align:start position:0%
The thing about Henry is once he has his
mind set on a particular course, he can

00:35:38.834 --> 00:35:45.354 align:start position:0%
be extraordinarily
cold and ruthless in achieving it. And

00:35:42.634 --> 00:35:50.674 align:start position:0%
anybody who gets in his way, well, they
need to watch out.

00:35:48.274 --> 00:35:54.594 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry tasks Wolsey with securing
permission from the Pope to end his

00:35:52.794 --> 00:35:59.074 align:start position:0%
marriage.
&gt;&gt; With the divorce, Henry gives Wolsey an

00:35:56.554 --> 00:36:05.514 align:start position:0%
impossible job to do.
Divorce isn't unheard of, but for a king

00:36:02.314 --> 00:36:09.874 align:start position:0%
to set aside a wife to whom he had been
married for 20 years, that doesn't

00:36:08.794 --> 00:36:14.354 align:start position:0%
happen.
There is no way that the Pope is going

00:36:11.794 --> 00:36:18.514 align:start position:0%
to agree. And Wolsey must be thinking,
I've got the boss from hell here. I just

00:36:16.554 --> 00:36:20.994 align:start position:0%
cannot deliver this. What am I going to
do?

00:36:26.874 --> 00:36:33.834 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Wolsey's attempts to secure a divorce
are failing.

00:36:31.434 --> 00:36:37.834 align:start position:0%
Losing patience, Henry takes matters
into his own hands.

00:36:35.794 --> 00:36:41.114 align:start position:0%
And he initiates a very public trial of
his marriage to Catherine.

00:36:41.434 --> 00:36:47.676 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; From Henry's point of view, the divorce
trial should have been a way to sort

00:36:45.596 --> 00:36:52.676 align:start position:0%
things out and get a legal ruling to get
his own way. But the [music] queen comes

00:36:50.476 --> 00:36:58.476 align:start position:0%
in. She gets down on her knees before
Henry, and she makes this extraordinary

00:36:55.116 --> 00:37:02.756 align:start position:0%
plea to her husband, asserting her role
as his wife, pleading for her rights to

00:37:00.916 --> 00:37:07.916 align:start position:0%
stay in the marriage.
&gt;&gt; He doesn't react. There is nothing. He's

00:37:05.756 --> 00:37:13.276 align:start position:0%
not at all swayed by all of this
emotion. This is an indication of that

00:37:10.516 --> 00:37:16.676 align:start position:0%
coldness just coming to the surface in
Henry's [music] character. It's almost

00:37:15.036 --> 00:37:20.276 align:start position:0%
like when he's decided that somebody is
no longer useful to him,

00:37:18.516 --> 00:37:24.516 align:start position:0%
that's it. He cuts them out. He moves on
to the next thing. It's almost

00:37:21.636 --> 00:37:24.516 align:start position:0%
pathological.

00:37:25.516 --> 00:37:32.516 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The divorce trial ends in failure.
And Henry blames his chief minister.

00:37:32.596 --> 00:37:38.236 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Wolsey has genuinely tried to get
[music] Henry the divorce he wanted. And

00:37:36.596 --> 00:37:42.236 align:start position:0%
it's not really Wolsey's fault that this
has not worked out. I mean, the big

00:37:39.916 --> 00:37:47.796 align:start position:0%
balance of power is against [music] him.
And yet, in Henry's mind, Wolsey has

00:37:44.876 --> 00:37:52.076 align:start position:0%
failed in the most significant diplomacy
that Henry has ever [music] asked him to

00:37:49.636 --> 00:37:52.076 align:start position:0%
do.

00:37:53.036 --> 00:38:00.716 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; There was this invisible line which
Henry drew. Once you crossed that line,

00:37:58.636 --> 00:38:04.796 align:start position:0%
you will pay the penalty for doing it.
And there's no going back. You can't rub

00:38:02.476 --> 00:38:09.396 align:start position:0%
out history. Once you have annoyed
Henry, once you have damaged his ego,

00:38:07.276 --> 00:38:15.201 align:start position:0%
you will pay for it.
And Wolsey knew his days were numbered.

00:38:13.181 --> 00:38:15.201 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:38:24.916 --> 00:38:33.836 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry VIII has turned his back on his
wife and his closest adviser.

00:38:31.196 --> 00:38:37.556 align:start position:0%
And strange quirks are emerging in his
character.

00:38:36.076 --> 00:38:40.716 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; If you actually met Henry VIII, it would
be important not to fix your eye upon

00:38:39.476 --> 00:38:43.956 align:start position:0%
him for too long or stare [music]
straight in the face cuz he he really

00:38:42.516 --> 00:38:48.077 align:start position:0%
didn't like that. It It was said of him
he couldn't hold somebody's gaze.

00:38:45.931 --> 00:38:51.917 align:start position:0%
[music] He felt uncomfortable.
This is one of the strongest kings of

00:38:49.837 --> 00:38:57.277 align:start position:0%
England, and yet there's a certain
personal insecurity, even when he's at

00:38:54.317 --> 00:39:02.317 align:start position:0%
his most secure.
&gt;&gt; Henry has this tendency to turn on his

00:38:59.717 --> 00:39:07.717 align:start position:0%
most trusted advisers. He puts them in
impossible positions, given these

00:39:04.917 --> 00:39:14.877 align:start position:0%
incredibly difficult tasks. And when
they fail, as inevitably they must, they

00:39:10.637 --> 00:39:14.877 align:start position:0%
get all the blame, not Henry.

00:39:19.077 --> 00:39:26.357 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry banishes Cardinal Wolsey for his
failure to secure a divorce from

00:39:23.397 --> 00:39:26.357 align:start position:0%
Catherine of Aragon.

00:39:27.197 --> 00:39:31.997 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; Once the king's most powerful subject,

00:39:30.037 --> 00:39:36.717 align:start position:0%
Wolsey is stripped of his post as Lord
Chancellor,

00:39:33.157 --> 00:39:36.717 align:start position:0%
and his property is seized.

00:39:37.077 --> 00:39:44.797 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; For Cardinal Wolsey, who always saw
himself as Henry's man, to have the king

00:39:42.757 --> 00:39:48.837 align:start position:0%
say that he didn't trust him, was
completely crushing.

00:39:47.037 --> 00:39:55.197 align:start position:0%
And from that moment on, we don't ever
really see him regain Henry's trust. He

00:39:52.197 --> 00:39:58.637 align:start position:0%
is just slowly sliding inexorably
towards his ultimate fate.

00:40:01.317 --> 00:40:08.597 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Wolsey sends Henry a letter begging for
his forgiveness.

00:40:06.837 --> 00:40:13.277 align:start position:0%
This letter, held in the National
Archives, gives an insight into Wolsey's

00:40:11.157 --> 00:40:19.037 align:start position:0%
desperation.
&gt;&gt; Wolsey is appealing so completely

00:40:16.117 --> 00:40:23.157 align:start position:0%
submissively to Henry in this letter
that it starts with,

00:40:21.117 --> 00:40:29.317 align:start position:0%
"I, your poor, heavy, and wretched
priest, do daily pray, cry, and call

00:40:26.437 --> 00:40:35.877 align:start position:0%
upon you." And then ends with, "Your
most prostrate, poor chaplain, creature,

00:40:33.637 --> 00:40:39.277 align:start position:0%
creature." I mean, not even a human
being anymore, just a sort of beast of

00:40:37.757 --> 00:40:44.197 align:start position:0%
King Henry VIII.
It could not be more clear in this that

00:40:41.757 --> 00:40:48.238 align:start position:0%
Wolsey is lowering himself in Henry's
eyes. It really is quite

00:40:46.157 --> 00:40:53.758 align:start position:0%
heart-wrenching, I think, that he was
reduced to this.

00:40:51.318 --> 00:40:58.318 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The cardinal's letter fails to win the
king over.

00:40:55.638 --> 00:41:02.878 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; I find Henry VIII quite challenging.
Because time and again, Henry can't

00:41:00.638 --> 00:41:08.198 align:start position:0%
admit himself that he's made a mistake.
He's completely certain that he is in

00:41:05.318 --> 00:41:13.678 align:start position:0%
the right at all times. And so, as a
result, the person who gets scapegoated

00:41:10.998 --> 00:41:13.678 align:start position:0%
is Wolsey.

00:41:16.198 --> 00:41:24.478 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry issues orders for Wolsey to be
arrested on charges of treason and sent

00:41:21.358 --> 00:41:24.478 align:start position:0%
to the Tower of London.

00:41:25.158 --> 00:41:28.518 align:start position:0%
But he will never make it there.

00:41:29.358 --> 00:41:36.078 align:start position:0%
After arriving at Leicester Abbey to
spend the night,

00:41:33.198 --> 00:41:36.078 align:start position:0%
he collapses

00:41:37.438 --> 00:41:40.278 align:start position:0%
and dies.

00:41:40.818 --> 00:41:42.838 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:41:50.478 --> 00:41:56.918 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; In the aftermath of Wolsey's death, one
of his servants goes to see Henry to try

00:41:54.838 --> 00:42:01.278 align:start position:0%
and persuade him to look kindly [music]
on his old servant.

00:42:00.118 --> 00:42:07.238 align:start position:0%
This is when we see Henry's
contradictory nature. Because Henry

00:42:03.878 --> 00:42:11.558 align:start position:0%
declares, "If I could lay out 20,000
pounds to bring back the cardinal,

00:42:08.984 --> 00:42:16.878 align:start position:0%
[music] I would gladly do it."
In the next breath, he reminds Wolsey's

00:42:13.958 --> 00:42:21.158 align:start position:0%
servant that his master had died whilst
owing him 1 and 1/2 thousand pounds.

00:42:21.429 --> 00:42:26.078 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; After Wolsey's death,

00:42:24.478 --> 00:42:31.258 align:start position:0%
it becomes clear that the Pope will
never grant Henry a divorce.

00:42:29.718 --> 00:42:35.558 align:start position:0%
But Henry is so determined to marry
[music] Anne Boleyn that he will stop at

00:42:33.318 --> 00:42:40.438 align:start position:0%
nothing to achieve it.
The next few years will see Henry make

00:42:37.878 --> 00:42:46.798 align:start position:0%
the cataclysmic decision to break with
the Pope and the Roman Catholic Church.

00:42:44.038 --> 00:42:51.438 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He didn't want to be responsible
to the Pope. He wanted to centralize

00:42:49.118 --> 00:42:56.480 align:start position:0%
power to himself.
&gt;&gt; That was the only way he would get a

00:42:53.280 --> 00:43:01.400 align:start position:0%
divorce. It was the only chance
of having a son and heir.

00:42:59.200 --> 00:43:07.480 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry has started to radically change
the course of English history.

00:43:04.080 --> 00:43:13.640 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He transformed every aspect of his
kingdom, religious, political, but he's

00:43:11.120 --> 00:43:17.400 align:start position:0%
developed into a very different man.
He's moved from being someone who's

00:43:15.140 --> 00:43:22.480 align:start position:0%
[music] a bit anxious and uncertain to
someone completely convinced of his own

00:43:20.360 --> 00:43:27.000 align:start position:0%
rightness, the justice of all of his
decisions.

00:43:23.960 --> 00:43:33.640 align:start position:0%
He was willing to change the entire
country, even the entire map of Europe,

00:43:29.360 --> 00:43:33.640 align:start position:0%
in order to get what he wanted.

00:43:35.200 --> 00:43:40.600 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; In the [music] next episode,
Henry turns on his new queen, Anne

00:43:39.240 --> 00:43:46.800 align:start position:0%
Boleyn.
&gt;&gt; The English court is a nest of hissing

00:43:43.440 --> 00:43:54.680 align:start position:0%
snakes. Absolutely nobody is safe.
&gt;&gt; This reads, "Her crimes were so

00:43:50.200 --> 00:43:58.600 align:start position:0%
abominable. Anne is the most wicked
queen in history."

00:43:56.560 --> 00:44:03.920 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; And Henry's [music] paranoia
begins to creep into England's politics.

00:44:01.880 --> 00:44:08.680 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry VIII [music] comes down on
opponents with murderous force.

00:44:06.640 --> 00:44:13.240 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; You're either with him or against him.
And if you were against him, you paid

00:44:10.760 --> 00:44:13.240 align:start position:0%
for it.

00:44:25.880 --> 00:44:27.900 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:44:31.120 --> 00:44:33.140 align:start position:0%
[music]

00:44:54.280 --> 00:45:00.281 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; You might think you know [music]
there is to know about Henry VIII.

00:45:00.841 --> 00:45:07.321 align:start position:0%
You'll know he married six times
and had two of his wives executed.

00:45:08.041 --> 00:45:15.716 align:start position:0%
But the truth about our most famous king
is much more complex and far more

00:45:13.601 --> 00:45:15.716 align:start position:0%
compelling. [music]

00:45:16.561 --> 00:45:24.281 align:start position:0%
This series tells Henry's story over six
of the most tumultuous decades in

00:45:21.121 --> 00:45:27.041 align:start position:0%
English history, separating the real man
from the myth.

00:45:28.641 --> 00:45:36.161 align:start position:0%
To some, Henry was a cruel bully.
&gt;&gt; He wanted the theater of punishment to

00:45:33.881 --> 00:45:39.641 align:start position:0%
be perfect. This is what happens when
you defy Henry. This is what traitors

00:45:38.241 --> 00:45:42.481 align:start position:0%
get.
&gt;&gt; To others, he was a charismatic and

00:45:41.761 --> 00:45:47.081 align:start position:0%
successful [music]
ruler.

00:45:43.841 --> 00:45:52.521 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He jousts, he rides, he sings. What more
could you want from this perfect prince?

00:45:50.081 --> 00:45:54.401 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But Henry's personality, his inner most
thoughts, and his motivations

00:45:54.306 --> 00:45:58.521 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; have remained elusive.

00:45:56.681 --> 00:46:02.001 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; When somebody is no longer useful to
him, that's it, he cuts them out.

00:46:00.201 --> 00:46:07.761 align:start position:0%
[music] It's almost pathological.
&gt;&gt; Once Henry has his mind set on an idea,

00:46:05.441 --> 00:46:12.561 align:start position:0%
he will stick with it, no matter the
consequences.

00:46:10.081 --> 00:46:17.521 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Now a team of Tudor experts have come
together to investigate who the real

00:46:15.081 --> 00:46:23.481 align:start position:0%
Henry was.
&gt;&gt; Here are Henry's insecurities

00:46:20.841 --> 00:46:27.321 align:start position:0%
written in black and white.
&gt;&gt; They'll unearth never-before-seen

00:46:25.092 --> 00:46:32.521 align:start position:0%
[music] documents, including some from
the Vatican's archives.

00:46:30.121 --> 00:46:37.441 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Thank you so much for showing me one of
the greatest prizes in Tudor history.

00:46:35.721 --> 00:46:45.121 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; And they'll go backstage at Henry's
court to unravel a murky world of power,

00:46:41.321 --> 00:46:50.201 align:start position:0%
plots, and petrifying ambition.
&gt;&gt; Henry VIII comes down on opponents with

00:46:48.521 --> 00:46:55.561 align:start position:0%
murderous force.
&gt;&gt; Henry's growing increasingly paranoid.

00:46:52.681 --> 00:46:58.803 align:start position:0%
He's starting to lose his grip on
reality.

00:46:56.441 --> 00:46:59.922 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry has got older, he's got more
tyrannical,

00:46:59.807 --> 00:47:04.442 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; his reign has got bloodier, and he is

00:47:02.162 --> 00:47:06.843 align:start position:0%
more determined than ever to get his own
way.

00:47:12.642 --> 00:47:21.043 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry VIII is now 41 [music] years old.
His first wife, Catherine of Aragon, has

00:47:19.122 --> 00:47:25.642 align:start position:0%
failed to provide him with a long-sought
son and heir.

00:47:23.843 --> 00:47:29.243 align:start position:0%
And he's becoming increasingly anxious
about the future of his dynasty.

00:47:31.362 --> 00:47:37.162 align:start position:0%
He's banished Catherine from court
and is embroiled in an attempt to

00:47:35.602 --> 00:47:42.283 align:start position:0%
divorce her
and marry his long-term mistress,

00:47:39.642 --> 00:47:46.083 align:start position:0%
Anne Boleyn.
&gt;&gt; The way in which Henry is treating the

00:47:43.963 --> 00:47:50.763 align:start position:0%
two women in his life could not be more
different. On the one hand, you have

00:47:47.963 --> 00:47:56.162 align:start position:0%
this great [music] chivalrous love play
with Anne Boleyn, and on the other,

00:47:53.122 --> 00:48:00.122 align:start position:0%
there is the incredibly cruel, heartless
rejection of Catherine of Aragon, the

00:47:58.162 --> 00:48:04.122 align:start position:0%
wife who served him loyally for more
than 20 years.

00:48:02.402 --> 00:48:08.203 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; It's interesting to think what it was
about Anne Boleyn that made her so

00:48:06.043 --> 00:48:11.442 align:start position:0%
attractive to Henry, but also so
enigmatically attractive to so many

00:48:09.922 --> 00:48:15.882 align:start position:0%
people.
Her education in France may have been a

00:48:13.642 --> 00:48:20.523 align:start position:0%
factor. She had a style and a glamour
that other people didn't.

00:48:18.642 --> 00:48:24.922 align:start position:0%
But also her intelligence, her ability
to argue with scholars and theologians

00:48:22.602 --> 00:48:29.083 align:start position:0%
about religious and moral issues.
Henry, the scholar, who flattered

00:48:26.963 --> 00:48:34.763 align:start position:0%
himself as being the philosopher prince,
saw in her, I think, a consort who

00:48:31.362 --> 00:48:34.763 align:start position:0%
shared some of those values.

00:48:36.922 --> 00:48:45.043 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But as their relationship develops,
Anne puts pressure on Henry by refusing

00:48:42.723 --> 00:48:47.723 align:start position:0%
to sleep with him until their wedding is
in sight.

00:48:47.763 --> 00:48:54.362 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Her own sister [music] had been
discarded as Henry's mistress. She

00:48:51.563 --> 00:48:58.682 align:start position:0%
wanted more for herself than that.
She wanted to be queen. [music]

00:48:56.003 --> 00:49:02.924 align:start position:0%
So, for seven long years, she keeps him
at arm's length, giving him a little bit

00:49:00.604 --> 00:49:09.004 align:start position:0%
of encouragement and then destroying his
hopes the next. That speaks volumes

00:49:05.444 --> 00:49:11.564 align:start position:0%
about just how much Henry was in thrall
to Anne.

00:49:12.004 --> 00:49:18.164 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's love letters reveal his
obsession with Anne.

00:49:16.244 --> 00:49:22.804 align:start position:0%
They survived to this day
and are held deep within the Vatican

00:49:19.979 --> 00:49:22.804 align:start position:0%
[music] library.

00:49:23.524 --> 00:49:33.204 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Luigina, thank you so much for allowing
us to film here and for showing me what

00:49:30.524 --> 00:49:38.684 align:start position:0%
has to be one of the greatest prizes in
Tudor history. These are the original

00:49:35.884 --> 00:49:42.724 align:start position:0%
letters from Henry VIII to his great
love, Anne Boleyn.

00:49:40.684 --> 00:49:47.684 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; You're very welcome and we are happy to
show people in Great Britain this

00:49:44.684 --> 00:49:53.724 align:start position:0%
document so precious to you and to us
and precious for I think all mankind.

00:49:51.444 --> 00:49:59.284 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's letters are written in French,
the language of courtly love,

00:49:55.964 --> 00:50:03.864 align:start position:0%
and are filled with romantic gestures.
&gt;&gt; You can see that in French, to my

00:50:01.444 --> 00:50:05.804 align:start position:0%
mistress there at the top of the page.
&gt;&gt; [laughter]

00:50:04.204 --> 00:50:09.724 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He wishes.
And you know, he talks about being

00:50:07.164 --> 00:50:14.564 align:start position:0%
struck by the dart of love or
dart d'amour. Now, this this is very

00:50:12.604 --> 00:50:18.924 align:start position:0%
famous, isn't it? The the love heart.
It's very romantic that he draws a love

00:50:16.644 --> 00:50:22.964 align:start position:0%
heart around Anne's initials and then
either side are his own initials. And

00:50:21.924 --> 00:50:26.364 align:start position:0%
even though we don't have Anne's
responses, we can sense that she's the

00:50:25.404 --> 00:50:29.484 align:start position:0%
one in control
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:50:27.084 --> 00:50:31.644 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; It's all Henry making the effort and
trying to woo her.

00:50:31.004 --> 00:50:34.650 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Yes.
&gt;&gt; And she's remaining just out of reach,

00:50:33.884 --> 00:50:38.924 align:start position:0%
which I think
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:50:34.964 --> 00:50:38.924 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; was part of her genius, actually.

00:50:39.324 --> 00:50:43.764 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The letters demonstrate just how
desperate [music]

00:50:41.724 --> 00:50:49.284 align:start position:0%
Henry is.
The longer Anne holds him off, the more

00:50:45.924 --> 00:50:52.764 align:start position:0%
insecure he becomes.
&gt;&gt; This is probably my favorite of the

00:50:51.204 --> 00:50:57.324 align:start position:0%
letters because I think it's the most
revealing of Henry's state of mind.

00:50:55.764 --> 00:51:03.765 align:start position:0%
You sense his insecurity in a way
because he talks of how he's been in a

00:51:00.244 --> 00:51:09.405 align:start position:0%
great agony uh since receiving Anne's
last letter, not knowing how to

00:51:06.685 --> 00:51:15.045 align:start position:0%
interpret it. Here is a man who has
showered his love with affection, with

00:51:12.685 --> 00:51:20.485 align:start position:0%
letters, with gifts. He's had very
little back. One of the naughtiest

00:51:18.005 --> 00:51:26.205 align:start position:0%
letters in the whole collection uh is
this one here where you really get a

00:51:23.045 --> 00:51:32.045 align:start position:0%
sense of Henry's frustrated lust. He
writes to Anne, "Wishing myself

00:51:29.605 --> 00:51:39.885 align:start position:0%
especially of an evening in my
sweetheart's arms, whose pretty duckies,

00:51:35.685 --> 00:51:43.965 align:start position:0%
or breasts, I long to kiss." It's really
quite saucy.

00:51:41.445 --> 00:51:49.085 align:start position:0%
Here's a man in torture through this
unrequited love. Anne's not giving him

00:51:46.685 --> 00:51:54.085 align:start position:0%
much back. Henry doesn't know where he
stands, [music]

00:51:49.965 --> 00:51:54.085 align:start position:0%
and it's sending him crazy.

00:51:56.085 --> 00:52:01.685 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Anne Boleyn's behavior and the desire
for a male heir

00:51:59.925 --> 00:52:05.565 align:start position:0%
have provoked Henry into making one of
the most monumental decisions in English

00:52:03.965 --> 00:52:09.885 align:start position:0%
history,
breaking with the Roman Catholic Church.

00:52:10.445 --> 00:52:18.045 align:start position:0%
Eventually, free from the Pope's
authority,

00:52:13.925 --> 00:52:18.045 align:start position:0%
Henry divorces Catherine of Aragon

00:52:18.125 --> 00:52:22.805 align:start position:0%
and marries Anne Boleyn.
But all of this

00:52:22.726 --> 00:52:28.005 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; comes at the highest imaginable price.

00:52:25.885 --> 00:52:32.725 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's break with Rome was probably the
most devastating political and religious

00:52:30.325 --> 00:52:38.205 align:start position:0%
and social event for 500 years. I mean,
suddenly to decide that England was not

00:52:35.405 --> 00:52:41.685 align:start position:0%
part of Catholic Christendom, to reject
the authority of the Pope and everything

00:52:40.365 --> 00:52:46.005 align:start position:0%
that that represented [music]
was something which disoriented,

00:52:43.405 --> 00:52:48.125 align:start position:0%
terrified everyone. The nation was
traumatized.

00:52:46.961 --> 00:52:54.485 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; Henry then declares himself head of his

00:52:50.805 --> 00:52:58.765 align:start position:0%
own Church of England.
&gt;&gt; For Henry to claim to be the head of the

00:52:56.165 --> 00:53:03.405 align:start position:0%
Church was unprecedented. It's very hard
to imagine the radical, shocking nature

00:53:01.285 --> 00:53:09.767 align:start position:0%
of that claim. A layman,
not someone trained in the Church, not a

00:53:05.927 --> 00:53:09.767 align:start position:0%
bishop, not someone in holy orders.

00:53:10.207 --> 00:53:16.327 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry believes this makes him second
only to God.

00:53:14.887 --> 00:53:20.167 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; On the one hand, you need to have quite
a big ego to deal with that. On the

00:53:18.607 --> 00:53:23.847 align:start position:0%
other hand, it's a great deal of
responsibility.

00:53:21.807 --> 00:53:27.927 align:start position:0%
Henry, who is already trying to manage a
kingdom, [music] is now trying to manage

00:53:25.647 --> 00:53:32.047 align:start position:0%
a church as well.
So, at the point that Henry breaks with

00:53:29.847 --> 00:53:36.407 align:start position:0%
Rome, I don't think anybody quite knows
what is going to happen next.

00:53:34.607 --> 00:53:40.487 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry might have got his wish to marry
Anne Boleyn.

00:53:38.007 --> 00:53:45.367 align:start position:0%
But this revolutionary decision is about
to catapult England into chaos. And

00:53:43.367 --> 00:53:47.887 align:start position:0%
damage Henry's reputation with his
people.

00:53:57.807 --> 00:54:05.167 align:start position:0%
England is in turmoil after Henry's
decision to break with [music] Rome.

00:54:02.807 --> 00:54:10.727 align:start position:0%
But despite opposition, he is now
ruthlessly forcing the new religion on

00:54:07.487 --> 00:54:10.727 align:start position:0%
his Catholic people.

00:54:11.447 --> 00:54:17.887 align:start position:0%
To push his religious revolution
through, he has a secret weapon in the

00:54:15.647 --> 00:54:21.007 align:start position:0%
form of his new chief adviser,
Thomas Cromwell.

00:54:22.527 --> 00:54:30.647 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Thomas Cromwell is nothing [music] less
than a genius. Talented lawyer, he's a

00:54:28.047 --> 00:54:34.927 align:start position:0%
property developer, a money lender,
trader.

00:54:33.247 --> 00:54:41.527 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But Cromwell is very different to the
noblemen that Henry's surrounded by.

00:54:38.567 --> 00:54:47.247 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Thomas Cromwell was the son of a lowly
person in Putney, just down the river

00:54:44.247 --> 00:54:52.727 align:start position:0%
from London. And he had this unique
ability to annoy people.

00:54:49.367 --> 00:54:57.847 align:start position:0%
Uh particularly the rich nobility of old
England, who regarded him as a common

00:54:55.207 --> 00:55:02.727 align:start position:0%
upstart because he wasn't from the great
and good families.

00:55:00.167 --> 00:55:07.928 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Men like Cromwell owe everything [music]
to Henry's readiness to put them in

00:55:05.407 --> 00:55:12.608 align:start position:0%
place. So, they really suit Henry cuz
they're going to be loyal to him.

00:55:10.648 --> 00:55:18.408 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry is really drawn to Cromwell. He's
got a cheeky sense of humor. He's not

00:55:15.328 --> 00:55:21.608 align:start position:0%
afraid of Henry, and as a natural bully,
Henry is actually rather disarmed by

00:55:20.568 --> 00:55:27.728 align:start position:0%
that.
&gt;&gt; He was ruthless, ambitious, and quite

00:55:24.928 --> 00:55:30.368 align:start position:0%
happy to tread on anyone who [music] got
in his way.

00:55:33.328 --> 00:55:41.008 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Cromwell seizes the opportunity to win
favor

00:55:36.568 --> 00:55:41.008 align:start position:0%
and hatches a plan to make Henry rich.

00:55:41.088 --> 00:55:48.128 align:start position:0%
He's worked out that England's
monasteries possess millions of pounds

00:55:45.008 --> 00:55:52.248 align:start position:0%
in untapped wealth.
&gt;&gt; Thomas Cromwell said, "I'm going to make

00:55:49.888 --> 00:55:56.368 align:start position:0%
you rich. Uh I'm going to dissolve all
these monasteries, and it's all going to

00:55:54.008 --> 00:56:01.528 align:start position:0%
go straight into your pocket."
Kings are always short of money, and

00:55:58.368 --> 00:56:06.408 align:start position:0%
that was music to Henry's ears.
&gt;&gt; Henry wanted to be the richest king in

00:56:04.488 --> 00:56:10.728 align:start position:0%
Christendom. It's all about his image
for Henry. He wants to have the most

00:56:07.888 --> 00:56:15.728 align:start position:0%
magnificent court to put one over on his
rivals such as the King of France.

00:56:13.168 --> 00:56:22.928 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; I'm not sure Henry's greedy. I think
that Henry feels that as king, it is his

00:56:18.768 --> 00:56:28.168 align:start position:0%
right to be in charge of everything.
&gt;&gt; To justify this money-making scheme,

00:56:25.648 --> 00:56:32.848 align:start position:0%
Henry and Cromwell start a slanderous
propaganda campaign against England's

00:56:30.248 --> 00:56:36.408 align:start position:0%
Catholic monasteries.
&gt;&gt; If you're going to dissolve the

00:56:34.048 --> 00:56:42.408 align:start position:0%
monasteries, you have to have an excuse
to do it. So, Cromwell and his agents go

00:56:40.208 --> 00:56:45.688 align:start position:0%
around, they start drawing up lists of
things that the monks and nuns are doing

00:56:44.328 --> 00:56:49.168 align:start position:0%
wrong.
&gt;&gt; Monasteries were always controversial

00:56:47.288 --> 00:56:53.528 align:start position:0%
places. You know, these were houses of
celibate men living on their own, often

00:56:51.368 --> 00:56:58.008 align:start position:0%
in remote, inaccessible places. Who knew
what they were doing?

00:56:55.928 --> 00:57:01.808 align:start position:0%
Protestant reformers are saying, "Not
only are these places of idolatry, but

00:57:00.048 --> 00:57:05.648 align:start position:0%
they're places of sexual sin. They're
sodomites, they're superstitious,

00:57:03.648 --> 00:57:10.088 align:start position:0%
they're monsters."
&gt;&gt; It's quite astonishing that the first

00:57:07.368 --> 00:57:15.729 align:start position:0%
piece of explicit legislation against
sex between men comes in in 1533

00:57:12.929 --> 00:57:20.169 align:start position:0%
precisely in the context of this
campaign. They find it useful to say,

00:57:19.209 --> 00:57:23.809 align:start position:0%
"You know what's going on with these
monasteries? All these monks are just

00:57:21.929 --> 00:57:27.089 align:start position:0%
buggering each other all day, all night.
You know, this is why we need a

00:57:25.089 --> 00:57:30.449 align:start position:0%
crackdown." And so they use this not
just to attack the monks, but to close

00:57:28.849 --> 00:57:35.609 align:start position:0%
down the institutions altogether. They
say things have got so bad

00:57:32.849 --> 00:57:35.609 align:start position:0%
they've all got to go.

00:57:36.209 --> 00:57:45.449 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Under Henry's orders, hundreds of
monasteries across the English

00:57:40.089 --> 00:57:45.449 align:start position:0%
countryside are pillaged and destroyed.

00:57:47.849 --> 00:57:55.009 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry [music] closed in the region of
563

00:57:52.249 --> 00:57:59.169 align:start position:0%
monasteries. That's an enormous amount.
These buildings had dominated the

00:57:57.089 --> 00:58:03.169 align:start position:0%
English landscape for centuries. They
were almost like the social services of

00:58:01.089 --> 00:58:09.409 align:start position:0%
their day, fulfilling the role of
hospitals, a charitable function.

00:58:07.089 --> 00:58:13.889 align:start position:0%
And so of course their loss had a huge
impact on Henry's people.

00:58:14.489 --> 00:58:21.049 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; This one report that suggests there's
20,000 monks and nuns wandering around

00:58:18.689 --> 00:58:26.929 align:start position:0%
the country homeless. That just gives
you an indication of how much of a

00:58:22.809 --> 00:58:31.689 align:start position:0%
shake-up of society this was.
&gt;&gt; Henry had pledged that all of the income

00:58:29.809 --> 00:58:39.129 align:start position:0%
from these religious houses would be
invested in creating new reformed

00:58:35.929 --> 00:58:42.729 align:start position:0%
religious establishments. He didn't keep
his promise. He gave away a lot of the

00:58:41.089 --> 00:58:47.809 align:start position:0%
riches, a lot of the lands to his
nobles, and he kept an awful lot for

00:58:45.009 --> 00:58:47.809 align:start position:0%
himself.

00:58:49.689 --> 00:58:56.849 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; 25 years into his reign, Henry has come
close to destroying the Catholic Church

00:58:54.649 --> 00:59:01.569 align:start position:0%
in England and made a fortune in the
process.

00:58:58.729 --> 00:59:06.329 align:start position:0%
But remarkably, in private, he's still
clinging on to the traditional Catholic

00:59:03.489 --> 00:59:10.289 align:start position:0%
beliefs that he grew up with.
&gt;&gt; There's a real contradiction in Henry's

00:59:08.169 --> 00:59:16.011 align:start position:0%
attitude towards the religious changes.
While in public he's outlawing all sorts

00:59:13.291 --> 00:59:23.131 align:start position:0%
of things such as going to mass in
private. That's exactly what he's doing.

00:59:19.771 --> 00:59:27.251 align:start position:0%
The Catholic mass is at the heart of
Henry's religious beliefs and really at

00:59:25.531 --> 00:59:32.411 align:start position:0%
the center of his life, and he attends
mass every single day.

00:59:30.491 --> 00:59:38.411 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; We know he crept on his knees to the
cross at Easter. These are in the views

00:59:35.891 --> 00:59:41.091 align:start position:0%
of most Protestants superstition.
But Henry was [music] convinced they

00:59:39.531 --> 00:59:44.691 align:start position:0%
weren't. Superstition were the things
that other people did. These things were

00:59:42.611 --> 00:59:48.131 align:start position:0%
true belief because in his heart he was
performing [music] them in the right

00:59:45.771 --> 00:59:52.651 align:start position:0%
way.
&gt;&gt; There is an enormous double standard

00:59:50.731 --> 00:59:58.971 align:start position:0%
with Henry. It's all very well for him
to continue worshiping as he likes, but

00:59:56.211 --> 01:00:04.731 align:start position:0%
his people have to tow a different line.
They have to be part of the new reformed

01:00:02.091 --> 01:00:04.731 align:start position:0%
religion.

01:00:05.291 --> 01:00:10.651 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But Henry's religious [music] hypocrisy
is testing some of his closest

01:00:08.931 --> 01:00:14.251 align:start position:0%
friendships.
To people like Thomas More.

01:00:14.531 --> 01:00:20.851 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Thomas More's relationship with Henry
VIII was as close to a friendship as a

01:00:18.451 --> 01:00:24.811 align:start position:0%
Tudor king [music] could have.
Uh they argued long into the night. They

01:00:22.771 --> 01:00:27.531 align:start position:0%
talked about the latest works of
&gt;&gt; [music]

01:00:24.931 --> 01:00:33.211 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; philosophy and religion. They went up on
the leads of the palaces and looked at

01:00:29.291 --> 01:00:37.931 align:start position:0%
the stars and talked about astronomy.
&gt;&gt; They'd first met when Henry was just 8

01:00:35.571 --> 01:00:42.851 align:start position:0%
years old. So, More was a huge influence
on Henry, and he rose and rose in

01:00:40.531 --> 01:00:48.391 align:start position:0%
Henry's service. He was Lord Chancellor
of all England by the 1530s.

01:00:45.851 --> 01:00:51.571 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But Thomas More was acutely religious.
&gt;&gt; [music]

01:00:48.611 --> 01:00:56.851 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Uh devout to the point of wearing a hair
shirt under his clothes so that his

01:00:53.651 --> 01:01:00.011 align:start position:0%
flesh was mortified by the irritant.
Maybe [music] he would beat himself with

01:00:58.371 --> 01:01:06.211 align:start position:0%
a a whip. I mean, these were the kind of
extreme religious practices that the

01:01:02.731 --> 01:01:09.251 align:start position:0%
most reclusive Catholics would use.
&gt;&gt; As a devout Catholic, Thomas More

01:01:08.491 --> 01:01:14.331 align:start position:0%
disagrees [music]
strongly with Henry's decision to break

01:01:11.691 --> 01:01:18.372 align:start position:0%
with the Roman Catholic Church.
And he's not the only one.

01:01:16.772 --> 01:01:22.172 align:start position:0%
Growing numbers of people are speaking
out against Henry's new regime.

01:01:23.092 --> 01:01:29.132 align:start position:0%
These voices of dissent play heavily on
Henry's insecurities.

01:01:29.852 --> 01:01:40.892 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Some outspoken priests in Middlesex said
that Henry's private life resembled a

01:01:36.412 --> 01:01:46.212 align:start position:0%
pig uh wallowing and defiling itself. A
nun makes these prophecies saying that

01:01:43.332 --> 01:01:51.132 align:start position:0%
she's seen a place reserved for him in
hell. For Henry, this is all deeply

01:01:48.932 --> 01:01:55.812 align:start position:0%
personal. Anyone who speaks out against
his reforms

01:01:52.612 --> 01:02:00.132 align:start position:0%
is criticizing himself, and he can't
take that.

01:01:57.172 --> 01:02:05.972 align:start position:0%
Like his father before him, Henry VIII
comes down on opponents with murderous

01:02:03.572 --> 01:02:10.732 align:start position:0%
force.
&gt;&gt; Hidden away in the Houses of Parliament

01:02:08.452 --> 01:02:13.412 align:start position:0%
is evidence of just how murderous Henry
is becoming.

01:02:16.452 --> 01:02:23.972 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Here I'm in the parliamentary archives
looking at the 1534 Treason Act, one of

01:02:21.252 --> 01:02:30.412 align:start position:0%
the most extraordinary documents in
Henry's reign. Here are Henry's

01:02:26.652 --> 01:02:34.252 align:start position:0%
neuroses, Henry's fears, Henry's
insecurities

01:02:32.012 --> 01:02:39.732 align:start position:0%
written in black [music] and white. The
1534 Treason Act says it's now high

01:02:37.172 --> 01:02:46.212 align:start position:0%
treason to maliciously wish, will, or
desire by words or writing, or by craft

01:02:42.972 --> 01:02:51.212 align:start position:0%
of to imagine an attempt bodily harm
against the king or the queen or their

01:02:49.052 --> 01:02:56.492 align:start position:0%
heirs apparent.
This document says that it's now high

01:02:54.412 --> 01:03:02.332 align:start position:0%
treason to maliciously publish and
pronounce by express writing or words

01:02:59.132 --> 01:03:06.772 align:start position:0%
that the king is a heretic, schismatic,
tyrant, infidel, or usurper of the

01:03:05.532 --> 01:03:11.412 align:start position:0%
crown.
The act is extraordinary because it's

01:03:08.532 --> 01:03:15.412 align:start position:0%
not only governing how people behave,
but it's governing how how they think

01:03:13.892 --> 01:03:20.773 align:start position:0%
and what they say.
Henry VIII believed that as far as his

01:03:18.813 --> 01:03:24.013 align:start position:0%
subjects were concerned, you're either
with him

01:03:22.213 --> 01:03:27.693 align:start position:0%
or against him. And if you were against
him, you paid for it.

01:03:28.213 --> 01:03:37.053 align:start position:0%
This document changed Henry's realm into
a land of fear.

01:03:33.733 --> 01:03:43.813 align:start position:0%
Words spoken in jest or in drink or in
anger could lead you to the scaffold.

01:03:40.933 --> 01:03:47.333 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; This brutal act significantly widens the
scope of treason.

01:03:45.533 --> 01:03:49.813 align:start position:0%
And it marks a turning point in Henry's
reign.

01:03:50.013 --> 01:03:56.493 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; That need not only to have people
obedient, but to believe absolutely in

01:03:54.933 --> 01:04:00.453 align:start position:0%
the justice of what he was doing was
unprecedented. No one had asked this

01:03:58.613 --> 01:04:04.373 align:start position:0%
before. That is intruding into
everyone's belief system, into their

01:04:02.133 --> 01:04:09.293 align:start position:0%
consciences, in a way that no one had
tried before or since.

01:04:07.453 --> 01:04:14.213 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; One of the first victims of Henry's
ruthless new regime is his old friend

01:04:12.053 --> 01:04:18.213 align:start position:0%
Thomas More.
Henry locks him in the Tower of London

01:04:16.293 --> 01:04:21.373 align:start position:0%
because More refuses to endorse his
religious reforms.

01:04:21.853 --> 01:04:32.373 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; More is very much a devout Catholic. And
that idea of England breaking completely

01:04:28.693 --> 01:04:37.493 align:start position:0%
away and defying the Pope, defying
tenets of Catholic faith is not

01:04:34.693 --> 01:04:42.413 align:start position:0%
something that More can really live
with.

01:04:39.813 --> 01:04:46.653 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; More remains in the Tower for a year.
And during that year, Henry does

01:04:44.253 --> 01:04:51.493 align:start position:0%
everything he possibly can to persuade
him. He even says to him, "Believe what

01:04:48.853 --> 01:04:55.813 align:start position:0%
you like in your heart so long as in
public you're with me."

01:04:53.693 --> 01:04:59.733 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; I think Henry still had that deep-felt
conviction that eventually their

01:04:57.573 --> 01:05:03.453 align:start position:0%
friendship would prevail and that More
would be won over by the sheer weight of

01:05:01.933 --> 01:05:06.413 align:start position:0%
argument and the force of Henry's
personality.

01:05:04.853 --> 01:05:10.653 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Tudor history is full of these moments
where people who have been working

01:05:08.373 --> 01:05:15.013 align:start position:0%
together for months and years suddenly
fall apart.

01:05:12.053 --> 01:05:21.013 align:start position:0%
But I think it's particularly traumatic
when it comes to Henry and Thomas More

01:05:18.133 --> 01:05:25.415 align:start position:0%
because of that deeper intellectual
connection that the two of them had

01:05:22.695 --> 01:05:25.415 align:start position:0%
forged.

01:05:26.135 --> 01:05:32.855 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Eventually, Henry has had enough and he
authorizes his former friend's death.

01:05:33.695 --> 01:05:40.695 align:start position:0%
The parliamentary archives still holds
the document that sanctions Thomas

01:05:37.535 --> 01:05:40.695 align:start position:0%
More's execution.

01:05:40.895 --> 01:05:49.495 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; This document says that Thomas More is
guilty of high treason by sowing

01:05:46.375 --> 01:05:55.655 align:start position:0%
sedition, by obstinately, contemptuously
refusing to take the oath

01:05:52.255 --> 01:06:01.775 align:start position:0%
supporting the succession to the crown.
They are powerful words. And later on,

01:05:59.095 --> 01:06:10.815 align:start position:0%
they describe the ingratitude
of Thomas More towards the king. It lays

01:06:05.655 --> 01:06:16.135 align:start position:0%
down Thomas More's crimes and legalizes
his execution.

01:06:13.575 --> 01:06:21.735 align:start position:0%
Into all intents and purposes, it's his
death warrant.

01:06:18.895 --> 01:06:26.295 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; On the 6th of July, 1535
Thomas More is executed on Tower Hill.

01:06:26.695 --> 01:06:32.895 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; I can't help but wonder whether Henry
just had those moments where he looked

01:06:31.695 --> 01:06:36.615 align:start position:0%
at himself in the mirror and thought,
"How on earth have I come to this?"

01:06:36.695 --> 01:06:44.735 align:start position:0%
Here he is
ordering the execution of some of his

01:06:39.855 --> 01:06:44.735 align:start position:0%
closest friends and advisers.

01:06:46.015 --> 01:06:55.975 align:start position:0%
He's caused turmoil in his kingdom. Did
he ever bring any of that back on

01:06:52.775 --> 01:07:00.575 align:start position:0%
himself and actually examine his own
motives, his own character?

01:07:01.735 --> 01:07:06.935 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; I don't think Henry had a conscience
&gt;&gt; [snorts]

01:07:04.415 --> 01:07:12.055 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; about what he was doing. No, he's not a
man who's going to lose any sleep over

01:07:09.135 --> 01:07:16.135 align:start position:0%
things like that. He has an objective
which he wants to achieve, the

01:07:13.535 --> 01:07:18.815 align:start position:0%
continuation of the Tudor dynasty, and
nothing or no one is going to stand in

01:07:18.215 --> 01:07:24.296 align:start position:0%
his way.
&gt;&gt; He absolutely believed in the

01:07:21.415 --> 01:07:28.296 align:start position:0%
righteousness of his own conclusions
and that's what drove him through.

01:07:25.896 --> 01:07:32.936 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; There's definitely a sense at this point
in Henry's reign that it's almost

01:07:30.296 --> 01:07:37.576 align:start position:0%
gathering a momentum of its own. There's
no stopping Henry now and it's going to

01:07:35.151 --> 01:07:42.216 align:start position:0%
[music] get more and more brutal.
&gt;&gt; Little does Henry know that a freak

01:07:39.856 --> 01:07:47.296 align:start position:0%
accident is about to alter the future of
his kingdom and the fate of his second

01:07:44.776 --> 01:07:47.296 align:start position:0%
wife.

01:07:54.146 --> 01:07:56.166 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]

01:07:59.496 --> 01:08:06.496 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry VIII is now 44 [music] years old
and his break with the Roman Catholic

01:08:04.296 --> 01:08:09.736 align:start position:0%
Church is beginning to tarnish his
reputation.

01:08:08.376 --> 01:08:14.576 align:start position:0%
He's desperate to [music] project the
image of a king at the height of his

01:08:12.016 --> 01:08:17.096 align:start position:0%
powers.
&gt;&gt; In the middle of the 1530s, Henry

01:08:17.072 --> 01:08:22.816 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; was a man increasingly obsessed by his

01:08:20.016 --> 01:08:28.176 align:start position:0%
public image. He would spend many hours
getting dressed by his men, covering up

01:08:26.136 --> 01:08:33.696 align:start position:0%
all those signs of weakness and
projecting this idea that here is the

01:08:31.456 --> 01:08:37.216 align:start position:0%
most magnificent king ever to sit on the
throne of England.

01:08:34.736 --> 01:08:43.056 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry from the beginning is very
conscious of the importance of the

01:08:39.296 --> 01:08:48.976 align:start position:0%
public eye but also he really enjoys it.
He loves performing to people, being the

01:08:46.296 --> 01:08:54.176 align:start position:0%
monarch. You have to look the part and
Henry [music] is particularly adapted at

01:08:51.096 --> 01:09:00.616 align:start position:0%
this. He's really interested in fashion.
&gt;&gt; So, we have records of Henry spending

01:08:58.056 --> 01:09:06.696 align:start position:0%
really huge amounts of money on cloth of
gold and he buys about 175

01:09:03.816 --> 01:09:16.216 align:start position:0%
pairs of shoes in one single 12-month
period. Henry is the ultimate investor

01:09:11.616 --> 01:09:16.216 align:start position:0%
in, dare I say, bling jewelry.

01:09:16.336 --> 01:09:23.016 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But beneath the royal clothing is a king
who is far more vulnerable than he

01:09:20.656 --> 01:09:26.858 align:start position:0%
looks.
Concerned he's losing the love and

01:09:24.737 --> 01:09:31.858 align:start position:0%
respect of his people.
Henry's propaganda machine goes into

01:09:29.058 --> 01:09:31.858 align:start position:0%
overdrive.

01:09:32.777 --> 01:09:38.697 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Having broken with Rome, it was really
important for Henry to win some hearts

01:09:37.097 --> 01:09:42.898 align:start position:0%
and minds if he's going to avoid a big
rebellion.

01:09:40.777 --> 01:09:46.817 align:start position:0%
It involves certain amount of PR effort
using print, which is a pretty new

01:09:44.657 --> 01:09:50.858 align:start position:0%
technology to produce lots of pamphlets
and trying to win back some of that

01:09:48.657 --> 01:09:57.058 align:start position:0%
popular support.
&gt;&gt; It's not easy to get a country to break

01:09:53.777 --> 01:10:03.137 align:start position:0%
away from a faith that it had as a part
of its way of life for centuries

01:09:59.657 --> 01:10:06.858 align:start position:0%
beforehand. So, that trauma of
separating from the Catholic Church is

01:10:05.298 --> 01:10:09.698 align:start position:0%
something that Henry has to respond to
directly.

01:10:13.578 --> 01:10:20.018 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Whilst Henry hopes to escape public
unrest,

01:10:16.778 --> 01:10:24.578 align:start position:0%
he can't seem to avoid it in private.
&gt;&gt; Henry develops an increasingly bad

01:10:21.978 --> 01:10:28.938 align:start position:0%
temper because he's losing patience with
Anne and with this marriage, and also

01:10:26.738 --> 01:10:32.258 align:start position:0%
the fact that he hasn't yet produced a
male heir. And so, he just now wants

01:10:31.177 --> 01:10:36.858 align:start position:0%
results.
&gt;&gt; Henry needs God to show him that he

01:10:34.378 --> 01:10:41.578 align:start position:0%
approves of his actions by giving him a
son.

01:10:38.218 --> 01:10:45.418 align:start position:0%
And yet, Anne does not produce a son.
She has

01:10:42.778 --> 01:10:49.738 align:start position:0%
miscarriages. She has a daughter. It's
as if his first marriage is is is just

01:10:47.738 --> 01:10:51.018 align:start position:0%
repeating itself.
And that worries him.

01:10:50.999 --> 01:10:55.698 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; What's wrong about this marriage? Is

01:10:53.097 --> 01:11:00.538 align:start position:0%
this marriage cursed as well?
&gt;&gt; As time went by, there were more reasons

01:10:58.378 --> 01:11:03.698 align:start position:0%
for them to dispute and argue with each
other.

01:11:01.657 --> 01:11:08.137 align:start position:0%
Her inability to produce the male heir
was the grumbling resentment, but also

01:11:06.258 --> 01:11:11.578 align:start position:0%
her commitment to religious reform, her
willingness to argue with Henry. These

01:11:09.938 --> 01:11:15.058 align:start position:0%
things were things that
over time became more annoying than

01:11:14.258 --> 01:11:20.578 align:start position:0%
attractive.
&gt;&gt; The real turning point for Henry is when

01:11:17.978 --> 01:11:25.578 align:start position:0%
Anne accuses him in public of having an
affair behind her back. And Henry is

01:11:23.418 --> 01:11:31.499 align:start position:0%
angered that she would dare question him
in public about his behavior.

01:11:29.019 --> 01:11:35.899 align:start position:0%
Henry responds to Anne by telling her
that she needs to turn a blind eye to

01:11:33.459 --> 01:11:40.339 align:start position:0%
this behavior as her betters had done,
meaning Catherine of Aragon, and that he

01:11:38.219 --> 01:11:44.939 align:start position:0%
could unmake her just as quickly as he
had raised her.

01:11:43.259 --> 01:11:51.019 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; There's another person causing trouble
inside the royal marriage.

01:11:47.059 --> 01:11:54.939 align:start position:0%
Henry's advisor, Thomas Cromwell.
&gt;&gt; Henry's court has become like a pressure

01:11:52.979 --> 01:12:00.659 align:start position:0%
cooker. So, at the center of this, we
have Cromwell and Anne who are each

01:11:57.259 --> 01:12:05.579 align:start position:0%
other's rivals and enemies.
Anne has her own faction behind her, and

01:12:02.979 --> 01:12:11.939 align:start position:0%
Cromwell has his supporters, and we see
in the court these two rival factions

01:12:08.099 --> 01:12:11.939 align:start position:0%
fighting for Henry's attention.

01:12:12.299 --> 01:12:19.019 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Cromwell knew that Anne Boleyn was
intent on having his head.

01:12:20.099 --> 01:12:29.579 align:start position:0%
So, he was very keen to act against her,
to strike first before he [music] was

01:12:26.459 --> 01:12:29.579 align:start position:0%
attacked himself.

01:12:31.339 --> 01:12:38.219 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Anne has an ace up her sleeve that she
thinks will secure her position.

01:12:35.859 --> 01:12:41.979 align:start position:0%
She's pregnant.
However, something is about to happen

01:12:40.219 --> 01:12:44.619 align:start position:0%
that will shake both Anne and Henry to
the core.

01:12:44.739 --> 01:12:52.539 align:start position:0%
When Henry takes part in the jousting
tournament, he falls from his horse.

01:12:50.699 --> 01:12:58.739 align:start position:0%
An account from the time
reveals that the accident is so serious

01:12:55.059 --> 01:13:03.779 align:start position:0%
that Henry is knocked unconscious.
&gt;&gt; There's a report [music] by Dr. Pedro

01:13:00.899 --> 01:13:08.339 align:start position:0%
Ortiz, who is the Imperial Spanish
ambassador to the Vatican. Uh he's

01:13:06.299 --> 01:13:13.739 align:start position:0%
picked up some gossip coming in from
Francis I of France, who's no friend of

01:13:10.899 --> 01:13:18.299 align:start position:0%
Henry VIII. The French king had said
that the king of England had fallen from

01:13:15.819 --> 01:13:22.219 align:start position:0%
his horse and had been for 2 hours
without speaking.

01:13:19.859 --> 01:13:28.619 align:start position:0%
So, here we have Henry lying on the
ground, not speaking for 2 hours. I

01:13:26.179 --> 01:13:32.380 align:start position:0%
believe the horse rolled on him, it
crushed him,

01:13:30.099 --> 01:13:38.500 align:start position:0%
and he suffered some kind of traumatic
brain injury. Recent research has

01:13:34.940 --> 01:13:43.740 align:start position:0%
demonstrated that such an injury can
actually cause neuroendocrine

01:13:41.620 --> 01:13:49.020 align:start position:0%
damage. People suffering from this very
rare disorder

01:13:45.460 --> 01:13:55.500 align:start position:0%
become depressed, irritable, and very
suspicious of everyone around them.

01:13:52.980 --> 01:13:59.020 align:start position:0%
In the latter years of Henry's reign, he
was displaying all those symptoms.

01:13:59.300 --> 01:14:07.860 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's accident also has a dramatic
effect on his wife, Anne Boleyn.

01:14:05.500 --> 01:14:14.260 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; What is [music] absolutely certain is
the shock of hearing that Henry had this

01:14:11.460 --> 01:14:18.860 align:start position:0%
accident caused Anne Boleyn to miscarry
a male child.

01:14:16.940 --> 01:14:24.980 align:start position:0%
Queen Anne was brought to [music] bed
and delivered of a man child before her

01:14:21.020 --> 01:14:28.860 align:start position:0%
time. They would say she took a fright.
It was a three-month-old fetus, male

01:14:26.900 --> 01:14:33.820 align:start position:0%
child, [music] perfectly formed.
Uh and and if the child had lived, it

01:14:31.980 --> 01:14:38.660 align:start position:0%
could have been Henry's
longed-for male heir.

01:14:36.500 --> 01:14:41.860 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The miscarriage is a personal disaster
for Anne because [music] that

01:14:40.100 --> 01:14:48.620 align:start position:0%
possibility that the male heir was
finally at last about to appear is taken

01:14:44.420 --> 01:14:48.620 align:start position:0%
away again, and she's damaged goods.

01:14:49.100 --> 01:14:55.380 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; After his accident, Henry becomes
increasingly paranoid.

01:14:53.781 --> 01:14:58.620 align:start position:0%
And at court,
things are now more dangerous for Anne

01:14:57.540 --> 01:15:01.781 align:start position:0%
Boleyn
and Thomas Cromwell.

01:15:03.340 --> 01:15:11.020 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; There is a diplomatic letter which
describes the English court as a nest of

01:15:08.900 --> 01:15:16.860 align:start position:0%
hissing snakes.
There are eavesdroppers at every corner.

01:15:14.100 --> 01:15:19.900 align:start position:0%
Absolutely nobody is safe from the queen
to the greatest statesman of the

01:15:18.300 --> 01:15:26.500 align:start position:0%
country.
&gt;&gt; Around Easter 1536, we see a real shift

01:15:22.860 --> 01:15:31.900 align:start position:0%
now between the relationship of Cromwell
and Henry. Henry calls out Cromwell in

01:15:29.660 --> 01:15:36.982 align:start position:0%
front of the whole court and publicly
disgraces him. And this now puts Anne

01:15:35.262 --> 01:15:41.582 align:start position:0%
back on the chessboard. And so, she's
removed Cromwell, her rival, and once

01:15:39.422 --> 01:15:46.342 align:start position:0%
again, she's the center of Henry's
world.

01:15:43.222 --> 01:15:51.062 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Cromwell storms out, and the first thing
he does is to start plotting to get rid

01:15:49.662 --> 01:15:57.342 align:start position:0%
of Anne.
Cromwell has decided it's Anne or him,

01:15:54.102 --> 01:15:57.342 align:start position:0%
and it's going to be Anne.

01:15:57.382 --> 01:16:06.142 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Secretly, Thomas Cromwell launches an
investigation into Anne's behavior.

01:16:03.742 --> 01:16:11.462 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; As soon as he's left court, Cromwell
puts the word out that he's sick. But,

01:16:08.582 --> 01:16:17.142 align:start position:0%
Cromwell is far from sick. He is using
this 2-week absence as the perfect cover

01:16:14.862 --> 01:16:22.662 align:start position:0%
for him to start plotting [music]
the downfall of his arch-enemy, Anne

01:16:19.702 --> 01:16:27.382 align:start position:0%
Boleyn. Cromwell has this incredibly
sophisticated network of spies and

01:16:25.422 --> 01:16:31.822 align:start position:0%
informants.
Among his network [music]

01:16:29.182 --> 01:16:36.822 align:start position:0%
are a number of ladies from the Queen's
own household. Now, Anne isn't popular

01:16:34.942 --> 01:16:40.862 align:start position:0%
with her ladies. She's a fairly cruel
mistress, so you might imagine how

01:16:38.942 --> 01:16:46.622 align:start position:0%
willing those ladies are to give
Cromwell little tidbits of gossip

01:16:43.502 --> 01:16:50.102 align:start position:0%
information that he can slowly craft
into a case.

01:16:47.622 --> 01:16:55.182 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; One of the things about the early modern
court is that [music] it is based upon

01:16:52.662 --> 01:16:59.342 align:start position:0%
flirtation, and it's based upon the
language of courtship. So, at any point,

01:16:58.022 --> 01:17:01.262 align:start position:0%
those acts which could have been
perfectly normal

01:17:01.078 --> 01:17:04.822 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; are reinterpretable as much more

01:17:03.022 --> 01:17:09.382 align:start position:0%
culpable. If you'd say you love the
Queen, what do you mean? Cromwell began

01:17:07.662 --> 01:17:13.022 align:start position:0%
to find a lot of evidence of people
saying inappropriate things.

01:17:26.502 --> 01:17:34.622 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Just 2 weeks later,
Cromwell presents his findings to Henry.

01:17:31.342 --> 01:17:38.183 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; When Cromwell had to go and tell Henry
what he'd discovered, it must have been

01:17:36.223 --> 01:17:43.903 align:start position:0%
the most terrifying moment of his
political career.

01:17:40.583 --> 01:17:47.623 align:start position:0%
To say that the king's wife, his queen,
was adulterous, I mean, that's not news

01:17:46.023 --> 01:17:51.023 align:start position:0%
you can slip in in a list of other
things as you're going through the

01:17:48.943 --> 01:17:54.583 align:start position:0%
morning's business.
&gt;&gt; Cromwell's evidence accuses Anne of

01:17:52.943 --> 01:17:59.023 align:start position:0%
conducting an affair behind her
husband's back with not one, but five

01:17:57.983 --> 01:18:02.663 align:start position:0%
men,
including her own brother.

01:18:03.423 --> 01:18:10.463 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; To be the king of England and to be told
that your queen is betraying you

01:18:07.863 --> 01:18:15.223 align:start position:0%
sexually is not something that you can
lightly brush off. He had to take

01:18:12.863 --> 01:18:19.623 align:start position:0%
control of that, and he took control of
it with a ruthless passion, a rage

01:18:17.714 --> 01:18:24.823 align:start position:0%
[music] that meant that it had to be
driven through, that there was no

01:18:21.223 --> 01:18:28.903 align:start position:0%
escape. This is a man not in denial, but
in manic acceptance [music] of the

01:18:26.783 --> 01:18:33.863 align:start position:0%
charge, and I think that's what drives
the process from there on in.

01:18:32.383 --> 01:18:38.583 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; When he wanted [music] something to be
true, it became true, and this was

01:18:36.783 --> 01:18:42.863 align:start position:0%
absolutely the case now [music]
with his second wife's infidelity

01:18:40.743 --> 01:18:47.663 align:start position:0%
because her real failure, let's be
honest about it, was not giving Henry a

01:18:44.863 --> 01:18:51.943 align:start position:0%
son. That was the only way she'd let him
down. I don't believe she was guilty for

01:18:49.543 --> 01:18:58.623 align:start position:0%
one moment of anything [music] else, but
Henry needed her out, and of course this

01:18:54.823 --> 01:18:58.623 align:start position:0%
was all too convenient.

01:19:01.023 --> 01:19:06.063 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; In the archives of the British Library
is a letter

01:19:04.423 --> 01:19:10.503 align:start position:0%
that provides a glimpse into Henry's
mind during this time,

01:19:08.383 --> 01:19:15.423 align:start position:0%
as well as the man manipulating him,
Thomas Cromwell.

01:19:13.263 --> 01:19:21.703 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; This is a letter by Thomas Cromwell
written in May 1536 at the height of the

01:19:18.943 --> 01:19:27.383 align:start position:0%
controversy surrounding Anne Berlin.
This letter is undoubtedly one of our

01:19:24.423 --> 01:19:32.423 align:start position:0%
best sources for understanding Henry's
perspective on Anne Berlin. Cromwell

01:19:29.863 --> 01:19:37.703 align:start position:0%
says here, "The King's Highness
thought convenient that I should

01:19:34.543 --> 01:19:43.905 align:start position:0%
advertise you of the same. I should tell
you about what's been going on about the

01:19:40.304 --> 01:19:48.945 align:start position:0%
case against Anne. Really, what he's
saying is the king has instructed

01:19:45.864 --> 01:19:52.905 align:start position:0%
Cromwell to spread the word about Anne
Boleyn's crimes, and they are all

01:19:50.945 --> 01:20:01.465 align:start position:0%
described here
in their full gory detail.

01:19:56.624 --> 01:20:06.824 align:start position:0%
This bit here reads, "Her crimes were so
abominable that I think the like was

01:20:04.824 --> 01:20:11.264 align:start position:0%
never heard."
And there's some

01:20:08.824 --> 01:20:18.065 align:start position:0%
fairly graphic language used here to
describe the queen's incontinent living.

01:20:14.425 --> 01:20:25.744 align:start position:0%
This is written for an absolute purpose.
It's telling the world Anne Boleyn is

01:20:21.184 --> 01:20:31.425 align:start position:0%
guilty of heinous crimes. Anne is the
most wicked queen in history, according

01:20:29.224 --> 01:20:35.824 align:start position:0%
to Cromwell.
&gt;&gt; Alongside charges of adultery,

01:20:33.624 --> 01:20:41.344 align:start position:0%
Cromwell's letter also accuses Anne of
plotting Henry's death.

01:20:38.664 --> 01:20:47.264 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; At the bottom, we have here talk of a
certain conspiracy

01:20:44.104 --> 01:20:53.905 align:start position:0%
against the king. So, in Henry's mind,
it goes beyond just adultery and an

01:20:49.945 --> 01:21:01.585 align:start position:0%
unfaithful wife. She's plotting treason.
This is a pure piece of PR on Cromwell's

01:20:57.824 --> 01:21:08.144 align:start position:0%
part. Cromwell manipulated Henry,
and in fact, he later boasted that he

01:21:05.104 --> 01:21:11.824 align:start position:0%
had dreamt up the whole scheme against
Anne Boleyn.

01:21:10.505 --> 01:21:18.344 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Whatever the truth behind the
accusations, Henry falls for them hook,

01:21:15.264 --> 01:21:22.945 align:start position:0%
line, and sinker.
&gt;&gt; Once convinced that there was a kernel

01:21:20.025 --> 01:21:27.664 align:start position:0%
of truth to it, Henry's imagination knew
no bounds. And at one point, famously,

01:21:25.425 --> 01:21:33.744 align:start position:0%
he said, "Well, maybe it's a thousand
men. Who knows what Anne is capable of?"

01:21:30.664 --> 01:21:38.985 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry VIII is a great fan of good
stories. He's good at spinning them, and

01:21:36.864 --> 01:21:44.466 align:start position:0%
he is also taken in by them. And the
story that is spun around Anne is the

01:21:41.906 --> 01:21:51.546 align:start position:0%
one of the wicked woman, a woman with an
insatiable desire to manipulate men.

01:21:49.106 --> 01:21:57.785 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry orders Anne's arrest, and she is
escorted to the Tower of London.

01:21:54.146 --> 01:21:57.785 align:start position:0%
He will never see her again.

01:22:08.825 --> 01:22:14.466 align:start position:0%
As Anne Boleyn awaits her trial in the
Tower of London,

01:22:12.225 --> 01:22:20.265 align:start position:0%
reports suggest that Henry VIII is
becoming mentally imbalanced.

01:22:18.265 --> 01:22:25.066 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The Spanish ambassador reported that
Henry had [music] collapsed in tears

01:22:22.146 --> 01:22:29.865 align:start position:0%
about Anne Boleyn's downfall.
&gt;&gt; Henry VIII was always an extraordinarily

01:22:27.305 --> 01:22:34.026 align:start position:0%
emotional man. Tears were never far from
the surface. Tears of joy, tears of

01:22:31.906 --> 01:22:38.546 align:start position:0%
grief. But, of course, Henry always
cries only for one person, and that

01:22:36.385 --> 01:22:43.305 align:start position:0%
person is Henry himself.
&gt;&gt; For Tudor men, not being able to control

01:22:40.785 --> 01:22:47.506 align:start position:0%
your wife is really seen as a cardinal
sin and the biggest blow against your

01:22:46.186 --> 01:22:51.785 align:start position:0%
masculinity.
&gt;&gt; I'm sure that Henry did believe Anne was

01:22:50.146 --> 01:22:55.745 align:start position:0%
guilty because it was convenient for him
to believe that Anne was guilty.

01:22:54.345 --> 01:23:01.026 align:start position:0%
And
it made him right. He was the good

01:22:57.305 --> 01:23:05.586 align:start position:0%
person. She was the bad person.
&gt;&gt; While Anne is under lock and key,

01:23:03.305 --> 01:23:10.586 align:start position:0%
the investigation into her infidelities
ramps [music] up.

01:23:08.066 --> 01:23:18.026 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; This letter was written by Sir William
Kingston, who was Anne's jailer at the

01:23:13.865 --> 01:23:24.026 align:start position:0%
Tower. And Kingston had been set upon
Anne as a spy by Henry. Henry wanted to

01:23:21.106 --> 01:23:30.186 align:start position:0%
know her every move, her every word.
Kingston reports this overheard

01:23:26.225 --> 01:23:32.986 align:start position:0%
conversation between Anne and Henry
Norris.

01:23:31.385 --> 01:23:36.906 align:start position:0%
Norris was actually one of the gentlemen
who served the king, but he was also a

01:23:34.865 --> 01:23:44.667 align:start position:0%
great favorite with Anne and stood
accused of adultery with her. Anne asks

01:23:40.785 --> 01:23:49.627 align:start position:0%
Norris why he would tarry before getting
married. Why is he waiting to get

01:23:47.027 --> 01:23:57.387 align:start position:0%
married? And she says the following
throwaway remark, "Did he look for dead

01:23:53.467 --> 01:24:02.027 align:start position:0%
men's shoes?" Effectively, she's kind of
teasing Norris saying, "Are you waiting

01:23:59.867 --> 01:24:06.547 align:start position:0%
for the king to die so that you can
marry me?"

01:24:04.107 --> 01:24:11.547 align:start position:0%
The fact that such a throwaway remark,
harmless in itself, was enough to

01:24:08.467 --> 01:24:18.667 align:start position:0%
condemn a queen of England shows you
just how febrile the atmosphere was at

01:24:16.467 --> 01:24:25.147 align:start position:0%
Henry's court. The king himself was
growing increasingly paranoid. He's

01:24:21.347 --> 01:24:32.027 align:start position:0%
starting to lose his grip on reality,
and that is all reflected here in this

01:24:28.347 --> 01:24:32.027 align:start position:0%
piece of evidence against Anne.

01:24:32.587 --> 01:24:39.867 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Based on this evidence, Anne is tried
for treason and quickly found guilty,

01:24:37.867 --> 01:24:42.267 align:start position:0%
as are the five men accused of sleeping
with her.

01:24:43.587 --> 01:24:51.867 align:start position:0%
Henry does not attend Anne's trial,
but he is heavily involved in the plans

01:24:48.627 --> 01:24:51.867 align:start position:0%
for her execution.

01:24:52.427 --> 01:25:00.747 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; So, Henry spends hours poring over the
details of the scaffold, how exactly she

01:24:58.707 --> 01:25:05.107 align:start position:0%
is going to die.
And he decides that he's going to have

01:25:02.387 --> 01:25:09.507 align:start position:0%
her beheaded with a sword rather than
with the traditional axe.

01:25:07.667 --> 01:25:14.267 align:start position:0%
The only woman in English history ever
to be beheaded this way.

01:25:12.627 --> 01:25:18.227 align:start position:0%
People have suggested that this was
because she was raised in France and

01:25:16.467 --> 01:25:21.147 align:start position:0%
that he was being kindly [music] and
thinking, you know, "Oh, this will be a

01:25:19.347 --> 01:25:25.827 align:start position:0%
lovely reminder of her childhood to get
her head chopped off with a sword rather

01:25:23.347 --> 01:25:30.147 align:start position:0%
than an axe." Or it was more dignified.
I don't think that's true at all. I

01:25:27.947 --> 01:25:34.987 align:start position:0%
think Henry was thinking about Henry,
not about Anne.

01:25:33.067 --> 01:25:40.907 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He wanted the theater of punishment to
be perfect. He wanted the execution to

01:25:37.507 --> 01:25:45.627 align:start position:0%
be exemplary. This is what happens when
you defy Henry. This is what traitors

01:25:43.147 --> 01:25:45.627 align:start position:0%
get.

01:25:54.549 --> 01:26:00.908 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry didn't ever [music] like to
associate himself with death. He

01:25:58.869 --> 01:26:05.309 align:start position:0%
wouldn't go to funerals, he wouldn't be
anywhere near anyone who was mortally

01:26:03.469 --> 01:26:10.469 align:start position:0%
sick.
And he didn't want to be seen in the

01:26:07.549 --> 01:26:14.428 align:start position:0%
same space as Anne Boleyn ever again.
Her name was not to be mentioned, all

01:26:12.229 --> 01:26:19.709 align:start position:0%
trace of her was removed from his
palaces. So of course, he's going to be

01:26:16.389 --> 01:26:24.349 align:start position:0%
nowhere near the Tower that day. [music]
But he invited a thousand people to

01:26:22.349 --> 01:26:29.829 align:start position:0%
watch Anne Boleyn's head being struck
off.

01:26:25.428 --> 01:26:29.829 align:start position:0%
Those are the actions of a madman.

01:26:30.389 --> 01:26:38.069 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; On the morning of the 19th of May, 1536,
Anne Boleyn is executed.

01:26:39.469 --> 01:26:44.229 align:start position:0%
But Henry has already lined up his next
wife.

01:26:45.908 --> 01:26:54.349 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The speed with which Henry moves on to
wife number three, Jane Seymour, is

01:26:50.629 --> 01:27:00.189 align:start position:0%
deeply disturbing, really. The very next
day they are betrothed, they're married

01:26:57.189 --> 01:27:03.989 align:start position:0%
10 days later. Now that is fast even by
Henry's standards. He needs to get

01:27:02.389 --> 01:27:08.509 align:start position:0%
cracking because, you know, he needs to
have a son and he needs to um

01:27:06.749 --> 01:27:12.589 align:start position:0%
live long enough for that son to grow to
adulthood. So he's not going to waste

01:27:11.189 --> 01:27:17.389 align:start position:0%
time
you know, pretending to mourn a woman

01:27:14.349 --> 01:27:17.389 align:start position:0%
who's betrayed him.

01:27:18.629 --> 01:27:24.229 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The following year, Jane Seymour is able
to give him what his two previous wives

01:27:22.948 --> 01:27:31.389 align:start position:0%
have not,
a healthy son, an heir to the throne.

01:27:28.549 --> 01:27:38.189 align:start position:0%
Tragically, Jane herself dies only 2
weeks after the birth,

01:27:33.829 --> 01:27:38.189 align:start position:0%
leaving Henry once more alone.

01:27:39.109 --> 01:27:43.269 align:start position:0%
But his reign is far from over.

01:27:44.349 --> 01:27:52.230 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The England of the late 1530s is
entirely different from the England of a

01:27:49.790 --> 01:27:57.590 align:start position:0%
decade before. We've got the monasteries
being dissolved. We've got a dramatic

01:27:54.830 --> 01:28:02.750 align:start position:0%
change of personnel at court. All sorts
of people have disappeared. [music]

01:27:59.790 --> 01:28:09.070 align:start position:0%
Thomas More is gone.
Anne Boleyn has gone.

01:28:05.550 --> 01:28:09.070 align:start position:0%
Jane Seymour has gone.

01:28:09.470 --> 01:28:16.070 align:start position:0%
Henry himself has got older. He's got
more tyrannical. His reign has got

01:28:14.426 --> 01:28:21.310 align:start position:0%
[music] bloodier, and he is more
determined than ever to get his own way.

01:28:19.150 --> 01:28:25.670 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; In the next [music] episode, age and
infirmity start to catch up with Henry

01:28:23.510 --> 01:28:30.270 align:start position:0%
VIII. The pain that Henry got from his
leg was absolutely huge.

01:28:28.230 --> 01:28:34.430 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; When the leg was really bad, he could
turn black in the face and just sort of

01:28:32.110 --> 01:28:37.590 align:start position:0%
lie still hardly able to speak.
&gt;&gt; And he turns [music] on his closest

01:28:36.390 --> 01:28:42.790 align:start position:0%
adviser.
&gt;&gt; Those less admirable traits that we'd

01:28:40.390 --> 01:28:49.350 align:start position:0%
seen hints of earlier in his life are
now front and center. This is Henry as a

01:28:47.230 --> 01:28:53.110 align:start position:0%
tyrant. This is the beginning of a
totalitarian state.

01:29:32.710 --> 01:29:38.790 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; You might think you know everything
there is to know about Henry VIII.

01:29:39.310 --> 01:29:45.910 align:start position:0%
You'll know he married six times
and had two of his wives executed.

01:29:46.670 --> 01:29:54.871 align:start position:0%
But the truth about our most famous king
is much more complex

01:29:51.552 --> 01:29:54.871 align:start position:0%
and far more compelling.

01:29:56.231 --> 01:30:03.072 align:start position:0%
This series tells Henry's story over six
of the most tumultuous decades in

01:30:00.831 --> 01:30:09.871 align:start position:0%
English history.
Separating the real man from the myth.

01:30:06.871 --> 01:30:12.631 align:start position:0%
To some, Henry was a cruel bully.
&gt;&gt; He's clever. What he likes to do is to

01:30:11.751 --> 01:30:17.991 align:start position:0%
trap people.
&gt;&gt; He's a very skillful manipulator.

01:30:15.471 --> 01:30:22.031 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's punishment was exemplary in its
brutality. [music]

01:30:19.711 --> 01:30:28.351 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; To others, he was a charismatic and
successful ruler.

01:30:24.991 --> 01:30:34.031 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He jousts, he rides, he sings. What more
could you want from this perfect prince?

01:30:31.351 --> 01:30:38.191 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But Henry's personality, his innermost
thoughts, and his motivations have

01:30:36.271 --> 01:30:41.711 align:start position:0%
remained elusive.
&gt;&gt; Henry didn't take the blame for his own

01:30:40.391 --> 01:30:45.072 align:start position:0%
mistakes, because that would not have
worked for him as a king. He was so good

01:30:44.422 --> 01:30:48.951 align:start position:0%
[music]
at convincing himself of what he saw as

01:30:47.471 --> 01:30:54.072 align:start position:0%
the truth.
&gt;&gt; Now, a team of Tudor experts have come

01:30:51.552 --> 01:30:57.351 align:start position:0%
together to investigate who the real
Henry was.

01:30:55.671 --> 01:31:01.751 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; If you ever needed proof that Henry was
a bit of a megalomaniac, this is it.

01:31:00.271 --> 01:31:08.031 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; And they'll go [music] backstage at
Henry's court to unravel a murky world

01:31:04.951 --> 01:31:11.951 align:start position:0%
of power, plots, and petrifying
ambition.

01:31:09.552 --> 01:31:15.311 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The English court is a nest [music] of
hissing snakes.

01:31:13.552 --> 01:31:18.951 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; No one quite knows who to trust. There
are spies and informers.

01:31:16.871 --> 01:31:27.072 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; It's very, very clear that behind this
public facade was somebody who was

01:31:22.072 --> 01:31:27.072 align:start position:0%
fundamentally vulnerable and insecure.

01:31:31.311 --> 01:31:38.471 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry VIII has [music] been on the
throne for 28 years.

01:31:35.871 --> 01:31:43.751 align:start position:0%
And the once carefree prince has become
a paranoid king, suspicious of everyone

01:31:41.391 --> 01:31:49.351 align:start position:0%
around him.
He's divorced his first wife.

01:31:46.351 --> 01:31:54.592 align:start position:0%
He's executed his second.
And his third wife has died after the

01:31:51.231 --> 01:31:54.592 align:start position:0%
birth of his only son.

01:31:55.673 --> 01:32:03.073 align:start position:0%
Now Henry is alone.
His controversial break with the Roman

01:31:59.552 --> 01:32:07.593 align:start position:0%
Catholic Church is making him unpopular.
And there are rumblings of dissent

01:32:04.552 --> 01:32:07.593 align:start position:0%
across his kingdom.

01:32:08.918 --> 01:32:15.153 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; Feeling increasingly vulnerable,

01:32:12.792 --> 01:32:20.193 align:start position:0%
Henry commissions a portrait designed to
promote himself as a formidable ruler.

01:32:18.743 --> 01:32:25.232 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; This is the iconic portrait of Henry.

01:32:22.872 --> 01:32:28.673 align:start position:0%
This is what everybody sees in their
mind's eye when they think of Henry

01:32:27.352 --> 01:32:35.352 align:start position:0%
VIII.
The silhouette of that figure could

01:32:30.752 --> 01:32:35.352 align:start position:0%
identify him just by itself.

01:32:35.392 --> 01:32:44.952 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; It shows Henry sure-footed, wide-legged,
staring straight at us. He looks like a

01:32:41.912 --> 01:32:49.832 align:start position:0%
mighty emperor.
&gt;&gt; It's no coincidence that the codpiece is

01:32:47.392 --> 01:32:55.432 align:start position:0%
at eye level. You you can't fail to
notice it. It's sending out a message

01:32:52.232 --> 01:32:59.472 align:start position:0%
that Henry is this great virile king.
Everybody knows all the problems he's

01:32:57.472 --> 01:33:04.153 align:start position:0%
had getting a male heir, but this
painting sets the record straight. None

01:33:01.432 --> 01:33:08.552 align:start position:0%
of that was Henry's fault.
&gt;&gt; The painting presents Henry as a

01:33:06.032 --> 01:33:11.832 align:start position:0%
powerful monarch in total command of his
country.

01:33:10.432 --> 01:33:14.633 align:start position:0%
But this portrait [music]
is a lie.

01:33:15.352 --> 01:33:23.792 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; That picture is propaganda.
We know that it's been changed to make

01:33:21.472 --> 01:33:32.472 align:start position:0%
his legs look longer, to make him look
more muscular. But in reality, Henry was

01:33:28.032 --> 01:33:37.032 align:start position:0%
slumping into geriatric decay.
&gt;&gt; It's an image of Henry that he wishes

01:33:34.352 --> 01:33:42.633 align:start position:0%
the world to see, not the actual Henry,
the sick Henry, the overweight Henry,

01:33:40.633 --> 01:33:47.232 align:start position:0%
the Henry that's suspicious about
everybody, and that's also feeling the

01:33:45.032 --> 01:33:50.673 align:start position:0%
effects of the infirmity of age, and the
oncoming march of death.

01:33:51.832 --> 01:34:00.274 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry is suffering from a painful leg
ulcer,

01:33:56.073 --> 01:34:00.274 align:start position:0%
which deeply affects his state of mind.

01:34:00.714 --> 01:34:08.954 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Sometime in the 1530s, Henry suffered a
jousting injury which caused a terrible,

01:34:07.234 --> 01:34:16.674 align:start position:0%
debilitating,
agonizing disease in both his legs.

01:34:13.554 --> 01:34:20.234 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Tudor medicine was rather basic.
So, his doctors advised that his wound

01:34:18.594 --> 01:34:26.314 align:start position:0%
would be kept open.
Which meant that he smelled. That his

01:34:22.034 --> 01:34:30.714 align:start position:0%
bed sheets stunk. His clothing stunk.
This is a man that you could smell

01:34:27.914 --> 01:34:34.354 align:start position:0%
before you saw.
&gt;&gt; The pain that Henry got from his leg was

01:34:32.434 --> 01:34:38.474 align:start position:0%
absolutely huge.
When the leg was really, really bad, he

01:34:36.834 --> 01:34:42.274 align:start position:0%
could turn black in the face and just
sort of lie still hardly able to speak

01:34:40.794 --> 01:34:44.754 align:start position:0%
for, you know, for several hours on the
trot.

01:34:45.194 --> 01:34:49.714 align:start position:0%
The infection had to be released.
[music]

01:34:47.914 --> 01:34:54.874 align:start position:0%
Which meant the leg often had to be cut
open and pus drained and ointment stuck

01:34:52.434 --> 01:34:54.874 align:start position:0%
on it.

01:34:55.234 --> 01:35:03.794 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; There was a lot of decaying flesh and
they wanted to remove that by

01:35:00.154 --> 01:35:11.234 align:start position:0%
cauterizing. Red hot irons applied to
these wounds in his leg. It must have

01:35:06.274 --> 01:35:16.154 align:start position:0%
been a living nightmare for him.
&gt;&gt; Henry's increasing infirmity, his

01:35:13.234 --> 01:35:18.754 align:start position:0%
ailments, had a profound effect on his
psychology. He couldn't cope

01:35:18.216 --> 01:35:22.714 align:start position:0%
[clears throat]
with the knowledge that he's no longer

01:35:20.354 --> 01:35:28.554 align:start position:0%
this kind of thrusting young king he had
been. He's turned into this incredibly

01:35:26.914 --> 01:35:35.514 align:start position:0%
vulnerable,
pain-ridden, old man.

01:35:31.794 --> 01:35:40.674 align:start position:0%
Henry's infirmity is laid bare when you
look at his private household accounts.

01:35:38.194 --> 01:35:45.034 align:start position:0%
So, there are these primitive lifts to
move Henry between the floors of his

01:35:42.514 --> 01:35:49.434 align:start position:0%
apartments. He's wheeled about in a
chair. He has a whistle to summon his

01:35:47.994 --> 01:35:54.474 align:start position:0%
attendants.
This is not the image that Henry wants

01:35:51.674 --> 01:35:54.474 align:start position:0%
for himself.

01:35:55.674 --> 01:36:01.915 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry thinks [music] that he knows how
to cure his leg ulcer better than his

01:35:59.676 --> 01:36:06.686 align:start position:0%
doctors.
A 16th century manuscript contains 32

01:36:05.075 --> 01:36:10.475 align:start position:0%
medicinal recipes
&gt;&gt; [music]

01:36:06.756 --> 01:36:17.196 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; that Henry concocted himself.
&gt;&gt; Most of his recipes are concerned with

01:36:13.876 --> 01:36:21.756 align:start position:0%
pain in the legs. So, here's a plaster
devised by the king at Oxford to ease

01:36:19.955 --> 01:36:26.435 align:start position:0%
the pain and the swelling about the
ankles.

01:36:22.955 --> 01:36:31.276 align:start position:0%
I would not use some of the ingredients
today. The king's [clears throat] gray

01:36:28.515 --> 01:36:39.955 align:start position:0%
plaster, for example, contains various
roots, flower buds, garden worms,

01:36:35.035 --> 01:36:46.796 align:start position:0%
scraping of ivory, and powdered pearls.
And finally, it also contains red lead,

01:36:43.716 --> 01:36:49.356 align:start position:0%
which is deadly poison. Do not try this
at home.

01:36:50.276 --> 01:36:56.115 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The exact nature of [music] Henry's
health has been subject to speculation.

01:36:57.676 --> 01:37:05.156 align:start position:0%
Recent research suggests that he suffers
from a rare condition which affects his

01:37:02.276 --> 01:37:05.156 align:start position:0%
mental [music] health.

01:37:07.915 --> 01:37:13.915 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Down the centuries, people have had lots
of different theories about what was the

01:37:11.995 --> 01:37:19.995 align:start position:0%
matter with Henry VIII.
I think Henry suffered from a hormonal

01:37:17.515 --> 01:37:27.156 align:start position:0%
disorder called Cushing's syndrome. In
20% of cases, it turns the victim into a

01:37:24.236 --> 01:37:32.716 align:start position:0%
suspicious person, wary of everyone
around them. They become melancholy and

01:37:29.796 --> 01:37:37.396 align:start position:0%
depressed, anxious. They can't take a
decision. They'll change their minds

01:37:34.196 --> 01:37:42.796 align:start position:0%
continuously. Now, all these symptoms
Henry displays in the latter years of

01:37:40.915 --> 01:37:48.955 align:start position:0%
his life.
&gt;&gt; Other historians attribute Henry's

01:37:44.595 --> 01:37:52.396 align:start position:0%
increasing paranoia to diabetes.
&gt;&gt; There's a lot to be said [music] for the

01:37:49.995 --> 01:37:56.356 align:start position:0%
view that as he became more and more
obese, he he he got type 2

01:37:54.955 --> 01:38:03.237 align:start position:0%
uh diabetes. I mean, it [music] can
start to affect your mind and you can

01:37:59.716 --> 01:38:07.516 align:start position:0%
develop elements of paranoia. And Henry
has elements of paranoia in these last

01:38:05.197 --> 01:38:07.516 align:start position:0%
years.

01:38:07.797 --> 01:38:15.516 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Whilst Henry's body and mind are
starting to fail, his enemies are

01:38:12.317 --> 01:38:15.516 align:start position:0%
gaining [music] in strength.

01:38:15.957 --> 01:38:21.797 align:start position:0%
There are reports of a huge uprising in
the north of England

01:38:19.837 --> 01:38:25.677 align:start position:0%
and Henry has [music] to act swiftly if
he's to keep control of his kingdom.

01:38:36.076 --> 01:38:45.156 align:start position:0%
Henry VIII is now 46 years old.
His painful leg ulcer has transformed

01:38:42.556 --> 01:38:49.757 align:start position:0%
the highly active king into a man who
struggles to even walk without

01:38:46.997 --> 01:38:54.156 align:start position:0%
assistance.
This lack of exercise, [music] combined

01:38:51.797 --> 01:38:56.957 align:start position:0%
with massive overeating, are making him
obese.

01:38:55.516 --> 01:39:01.036 align:start position:0%
And there are detailed records of the
enormous [music] quantities of food he

01:38:58.757 --> 01:39:04.116 align:start position:0%
eats.
&gt;&gt; Here we have an example of what Henry

01:39:02.757 --> 01:39:08.556 align:start position:0%
would be eating
on pretty much any given day of the

01:39:06.237 --> 01:39:14.877 align:start position:0%
week. We have everything from swan and
custard through to rich roasted baby kid

01:39:12.837 --> 01:39:19.516 align:start position:0%
or lamb. There's butter and eggs,
there's jelly and hippocras,

01:39:17.277 --> 01:39:24.237 align:start position:0%
porpoise and seal for the king's
delight. But it's been estimated that

01:39:21.957 --> 01:39:28.357 align:start position:0%
King Henry VIII would have been having
about double the number of calories,

01:39:26.277 --> 01:39:32.837 align:start position:0%
bare minimum, that you would recommend
in the 21st century.

01:39:30.757 --> 01:39:37.237 align:start position:0%
Because Henry was eating so much meat,
he inevitably suffered severe

01:39:35.036 --> 01:39:40.717 align:start position:0%
constipation. And there's an account in
the letters and papers of King Henry

01:39:38.596 --> 01:39:44.596 align:start position:0%
VIII of how one of Henry's physicians
actually had to come and administer a

01:39:42.596 --> 01:39:48.997 align:start position:0%
clyster, that is an enema as we'd call
it today, to the king in order to try

01:39:46.677 --> 01:39:52.397 align:start position:0%
and flush out his system. And the
document goes on to proudly report how

01:39:51.116 --> 01:39:56.477 align:start position:0%
the king got up in the middle of the
night and had a fair siege on the

01:39:54.357 --> 01:40:00.516 align:start position:0%
toilet. Delightful for all those around
him, obviously.

01:39:58.156 --> 01:40:06.158 align:start position:0%
Henry always saw himself as that
beautiful young prince he had been once,

01:40:03.317 --> 01:40:10.518 align:start position:0%
universally adored as a sportsman, an
athlete, a Renaissance prince. And I

01:40:08.638 --> 01:40:14.918 align:start position:0%
think he found it very difficult towards
the end of his life, as what he saw in

01:40:12.358 --> 01:40:20.478 align:start position:0%
the mirror was no longer that handsome
young man, but instead undeniably a sort

01:40:18.038 --> 01:40:23.238 align:start position:0%
of slightly hideous sort of old
creature.

01:40:25.038 --> 01:40:30.598 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; It's 3 years since Henry broke [music]
with the Roman Catholic Church and

01:40:28.838 --> 01:40:33.158 align:start position:0%
declared himself head of the Church of
England.

01:40:34.278 --> 01:40:39.169 align:start position:0%
But now the repercussions of his
religious revolution are catching up

01:40:38.038 --> 01:40:44.278 align:start position:0%
with him.
&gt;&gt; [cheering]

01:40:40.998 --> 01:40:47.718 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; This radical move is extremely unpopular
and results in a religious uprising in

01:40:46.078 --> 01:40:54.318 align:start position:0%
the north of England
known as the Pilgrimage of Grace.

01:40:51.998 --> 01:40:59.758 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; This was the first major rebellion
against Henry's reformation and it

01:40:56.678 --> 01:41:04.878 align:start position:0%
shocked him to the core because he was
so good at convincing himself of what he

01:41:03.238 --> 01:41:10.198 align:start position:0%
saw as the truth. He thought his people
still loved him.

01:41:06.678 --> 01:41:14.678 align:start position:0%
This now changed everything.
The whole point of the Tudors were that

01:41:11.838 --> 01:41:20.598 align:start position:0%
they brought peace and union to England
after the divisions of the Wars of the

01:41:16.438 --> 01:41:25.438 align:start position:0%
Roses and now you have division again.
This is an epic failure of kingship and

01:41:23.358 --> 01:41:31.638 align:start position:0%
Henry understands that and he is
extremely concerned.

01:41:28.998 --> 01:41:36.278 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But with no army at his disposal, Henry
is unable to defeat the rebellion

01:41:32.880 --> 01:41:41.278 align:start position:0%
[music] with brute force.
&gt;&gt; Kings of England never had standing

01:41:37.758 --> 01:41:45.278 align:start position:0%
armies, so they had to rule with the
consent of the people. He realized that

01:41:44.078 --> 01:41:48.878 align:start position:0%
he was
he was in a very dangerous situation now

01:41:47.118 --> 01:41:54.878 align:start position:0%
and he needed to act tactically,
politically and this is what he did.

01:41:52.758 --> 01:41:58.518 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry comes up with a plan to deal with
the rebels.

01:41:56.558 --> 01:42:03.918 align:start position:0%
He offers them a pardon and invites
their ringleader, Robert Aske, to a

01:42:00.918 --> 01:42:03.918 align:start position:0%
secret meeting.

01:42:04.278 --> 01:42:08.919 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry has this master stroke. I mean, he
invites Robert Aske and [music] the

01:42:07.159 --> 01:42:14.479 align:start position:0%
leaders of the pilgrimage to court and
he entertains them for Christmas. He

01:42:11.159 --> 01:42:19.599 align:start position:0%
gives them gifts and looks after them.
&gt;&gt; Aske went away very happy saying that

01:42:16.759 --> 01:42:27.679 align:start position:0%
he'd enjoyed every sign of the king's
grace, of his mercy. What a fantastic

01:42:23.519 --> 01:42:33.519 align:start position:0%
king Aske is essentially saying.
&gt;&gt; But it soon becomes clear that Henry's

01:42:29.639 --> 01:42:37.959 align:start position:0%
show of mercy is a trick.
And he turns on the rebels with a

01:42:35.106 --> 01:42:41.359 align:start position:0%
[music] vengeance.
&gt;&gt; Henry was the sort of ruler who would

01:42:39.559 --> 01:42:45.959 align:start position:0%
gallop you along and then basically cut
you off. He's clever. But what he likes

01:42:43.759 --> 01:42:48.861 align:start position:0%
to do is to try and trap people, move
them about on the chessboard. He's a

01:42:47.559 --> 01:42:51.999 align:start position:0%
very skillful
&gt;&gt; [music]

01:42:49.159 --> 01:42:51.999 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; manipulator.

01:42:53.159 --> 01:43:00.879 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Robert Aske returns home
and Henry orders his arrest and

01:42:58.439 --> 01:43:04.919 align:start position:0%
execution.
&gt;&gt; Henry's punishment of Robert Aske was

01:43:02.879 --> 01:43:10.599 align:start position:0%
exemplary in its brutality.
&gt;&gt; And he was hung up for days, asphyxiated

01:43:07.439 --> 01:43:14.919 align:start position:0%
under the weight of his own body.
&gt;&gt; This is a message to the people that

01:43:13.479 --> 01:43:15.759 align:start position:0%
this is what happens when you oppose
Henry.

01:43:15.716 --> 01:43:20.359 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; And in fact, he wanted to go much

01:43:17.679 --> 01:43:24.639 align:start position:0%
further. He wanted people from every
village involved in the rebellion to

01:43:22.079 --> 01:43:29.079 align:start position:0%
have somebody executed.
But the man who was in charge of the

01:43:27.039 --> 01:43:31.919 align:start position:0%
retaliation simply didn't carry out
Henry's orders.

01:43:32.479 --> 01:43:38.639 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's ruthless suppression of the
rebels marks a turning point in his

01:43:36.439 --> 01:43:42.919 align:start position:0%
reign.
&gt;&gt; England had changed an awful lot during

01:43:40.879 --> 01:43:48.239 align:start position:0%
this period. It was no longer the merry
England of Henry's early years. It was

01:43:45.239 --> 01:43:52.599 align:start position:0%
now pretty much a totalitarian state.
There were spies everywhere.

01:43:50.279 --> 01:43:57.079 align:start position:0%
Suddenly, nobody was safe. Nobody could
trust anyone. There were neighbors

01:43:54.919 --> 01:44:02.039 align:start position:0%
informing on neighbors.
So, you never knew when there was going

01:43:58.519 --> 01:44:02.039 align:start position:0%
to be that knock on the door.

01:44:03.279 --> 01:44:10.721 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; People were now afraid to open their
mouths in any public place. People were

01:44:08.679 --> 01:44:16.081 align:start position:0%
afraid to write letters and express an
opinion because they were always looking

01:44:13.041 --> 01:44:16.081 align:start position:0%
over their shoulder.

01:44:18.921 --> 01:44:26.721 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The man responsible for enacting Henry's
crackdowns is his chief minister, Thomas

01:44:24.121 --> 01:44:26.721 align:start position:0%
Cromwell.

01:44:27.561 --> 01:44:33.321 align:start position:0%
Cromwell has previously masterminded the
breakup [music] of the monasteries and

01:44:31.641 --> 01:44:37.321 align:start position:0%
engineered the downfall of Henry's
second wife, Anne Boleyn.

01:44:37.601 --> 01:44:41.641 align:start position:0%
But now that Henry's people are turning
on him,

01:44:40.281 --> 01:44:44.201 align:start position:0%
he shifts the blame [music] onto
Cromwell.

01:44:44.361 --> 01:44:49.841 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry didn't take the blame for his own
mistakes because that would not have

01:44:47.721 --> 01:44:53.681 align:start position:0%
worked for him as a king.
One of the purposes of good servants was

01:44:51.721 --> 01:44:58.081 align:start position:0%
that they would take the blame if things
went wrong. It was their advice.

01:44:56.521 --> 01:45:01.281 align:start position:0%
With the Pilgrimage of Grace, they
didn't attack Henry so much, they

01:44:59.441 --> 01:45:04.721 align:start position:0%
attacked Cromwell.
&gt;&gt; There is definitely a sense in which

01:45:02.841 --> 01:45:08.521 align:start position:0%
Thomas Cromwell is Henry VIII's
scapegoat. Henry could step back and

01:45:06.641 --> 01:45:12.121 align:start position:0%
say, "I'm innocent of this. I don't know
what's going on. I don't know what my

01:45:10.041 --> 01:45:17.361 align:start position:0%
servants are doing. And now that I found
out, I'm absolutely appalled."

01:45:15.281 --> 01:45:21.441 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; There had been warning signs for
Cromwell for a few years now that

01:45:18.961 --> 01:45:25.921 align:start position:0%
actually his luck was changing. There
were arguments with the king and in fact

01:45:24.121 --> 01:45:32.641 align:start position:0%
on a number of occasions the king was
said to have been naveous Cromwell. He

01:45:28.921 --> 01:45:38.721 align:start position:0%
was beating him up in front of the court
on one occasion pommeling him about the

01:45:35.201 --> 01:45:41.921 align:start position:0%
head as if he were a dog. Cromwell must
have been terrified.

01:45:43.121 --> 01:45:49.361 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; As he starts to fall out of favor,
Cromwell is given the chance to redeem

01:45:47.161 --> 01:45:54.081 align:start position:0%
himself.
It's been 2 years since the death of

01:45:51.001 --> 01:45:59.121 align:start position:0%
Henry's great love, Jane Seymour.
And now Cromwell is tasked with finding

01:45:56.441 --> 01:46:03.041 align:start position:0%
him a new wife.
&gt;&gt; He's now got the heir, but you know, he

01:46:01.081 --> 01:46:07.601 align:start position:0%
doesn't have the spare. And Henry is
deeply skeptical about female monarchy.

01:46:05.361 --> 01:46:10.801 align:start position:0%
He's not excited about the prospect of
either of his daughters becoming his

01:46:09.601 --> 01:46:15.602 align:start position:0%
successor.
So, he's looking for a new wife to

01:46:12.602 --> 01:46:15.602 align:start position:0%
produce sons.

01:46:15.922 --> 01:46:23.562 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Cromwell strikes a political deal for
Henry to marry the German noblewoman

01:46:20.682 --> 01:46:29.122 align:start position:0%
Anne of Cleves.
And Henry agrees to marry her based

01:46:25.802 --> 01:46:33.482 align:start position:0%
solely on seeing her portrait.
&gt;&gt; Well, he sees an image of a girl who

01:46:30.562 --> 01:46:38.403 align:start position:0%
looks like a doll. She's pretty, she's
young, she looks very unthreatening.

01:46:39.002 --> 01:46:45.282 align:start position:0%
So, Henry sees the portrait and he
thinks, "Well, she looks a bit of all

01:46:42.722 --> 01:46:48.642 align:start position:0%
right. Um I'll I'll go for that. Yep,
that seems that's fine."

01:46:49.122 --> 01:46:55.922 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But when Henry meets Anne in person,
he changes his mind completely.

01:46:56.122 --> 01:47:02.202 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; When Anne arrives, she's put up in
Rochester Castle and Henry can't wait to

01:47:00.363 --> 01:47:05.682 align:start position:0%
see her, so he goes in disguise with a
gift to basically have a quick peep. But

01:47:04.442 --> 01:47:10.002 align:start position:0%
actually, Anne doesn't really take any
notice of this rather obese uh stranger

01:47:08.082 --> 01:47:13.282 align:start position:0%
who sort of pops by and um that that's
not a good start.

01:47:11.522 --> 01:47:18.323 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Poor Anne of Cleves was dressed in the
most hideous German costume, a sort of

01:47:15.843 --> 01:47:23.323 align:start position:0%
contrasting bands of fabric and a sort
of helmet that looks like something out

01:47:20.562 --> 01:47:29.002 align:start position:0%
of Star Wars. And uh he was horribly
disappointed.

01:47:25.682 --> 01:47:34.843 align:start position:0%
Henry made his revulsion towards Anne of
Cleves absolutely clear. He complained

01:47:31.883 --> 01:47:39.282 align:start position:0%
that there were "Displeasant airs about
her." And there's a very lurid

01:47:36.642 --> 01:47:42.602 align:start position:0%
description of their wedding night where
Henry is said to have run his hands all

01:47:41.122 --> 01:47:48.002 align:start position:0%
over his wife's body, feeling her
breasts and her belly, and it gave him

01:47:45.282 --> 01:47:53.762 align:start position:0%
enough of a conviction to declare that
she was no maid. She hadn't come to him

01:47:50.802 --> 01:47:53.762 align:start position:0%
a virgin.

01:47:54.722 --> 01:48:01.282 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's smear campaign against Anne of
Cleves actually reveals more about his

01:47:59.042 --> 01:48:06.202 align:start position:0%
own personal insecurities than anything
else.

01:48:03.482 --> 01:48:11.122 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry has for some time been suffering
from bouts of impotence,

01:48:08.403 --> 01:48:15.924 align:start position:0%
and he finds himself unable to
consummate the marriage. I think perhaps

01:48:13.403 --> 01:48:20.163 align:start position:0%
he has a a bit of a go, it doesn't work
out, and then he decides, "This is not

01:48:17.523 --> 01:48:20.163 align:start position:0%
my fault."

01:48:20.283 --> 01:48:24.484 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry [music]
said that he was capable of having sex

01:48:22.683 --> 01:48:27.924 align:start position:0%
with other women, that he was still
having wet dreams. He absolutely

01:48:26.043 --> 01:48:31.844 align:start position:0%
insisted that that was known by everyone
around the court. Really, it undermined

01:48:30.163 --> 01:48:35.163 align:start position:0%
his masculinity that he couldn't have
sex with his own wife, but he was not

01:48:33.683 --> 01:48:39.563 align:start position:0%
willing to acknowledge that it was his
problem. As far as he was concerned, it

01:48:36.884 --> 01:48:39.563 align:start position:0%
was her.

01:48:40.523 --> 01:48:47.723 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's PR campaign against Anne was so
effective that even centuries later,

01:48:45.884 --> 01:48:52.364 align:start position:0%
there's a tendency to still refer to her
as the Flanders mare, the ugly wife whom

01:48:50.484 --> 01:48:58.203 align:start position:0%
he was lucky enough to get rid of quite
quickly. We completely overlook the fact

01:48:56.683 --> 01:49:04.723 align:start position:0%
that actually there was probably nothing
wrong with Anne, and frankly, Henry was

01:49:01.004 --> 01:49:04.723 align:start position:0%
no oil painting by this time.

01:49:07.203 --> 01:49:13.523 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The Anne of Cleves marriage is an
unmitigated disaster.

01:49:11.484 --> 01:49:18.884 align:start position:0%
And Henry lays the blame squarely at
Cromwell's feet.

01:49:16.484 --> 01:49:23.803 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; I don't think Henry really turns against
Cromwell until the Cleves marriage. When

01:49:21.283 --> 01:49:29.243 align:start position:0%
Henry feels that somebody has disobeyed
him or has been working against him, he

01:49:27.444 --> 01:49:33.404 align:start position:0%
feels that the scales have fallen from
his eyes, and he's going to do something

01:49:31.123 --> 01:49:37.203 align:start position:0%
about it. And so, he will cut them off.
And, you know, he's got this infinite

01:49:35.163 --> 01:49:42.723 align:start position:0%
talent for turning loyal servants into
enemies of the state, and Cromwell falls

01:49:39.404 --> 01:49:47.404 align:start position:0%
into [music] that bracket.
&gt;&gt; Seeking to exploit the growing rift

01:49:44.884 --> 01:49:51.404 align:start position:0%
between Henry and Cromwell, Cromwell's
enemies at court start to plot against

01:49:49.844 --> 01:49:54.723 align:start position:0%
him.
Chief among these enemies is Thomas

01:49:53.683 --> 01:49:58.683 align:start position:0%
Howard,
the Duke of Norfolk.

01:49:57.203 --> 01:50:02.444 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Well, Thomas Howard, third Duke of
Norfolk, is one of the most unpleasant

01:50:00.603 --> 01:50:09.643 align:start position:0%
men in English history. He was
ambitious, vain, arrogant. For Norfolk,

01:50:06.603 --> 01:50:14.603 align:start position:0%
Thomas Cromwell was public enemy number
one. Norfolk thinks that Cromwell's too

01:50:12.924 --> 01:50:17.965 align:start position:0%
big [music] for his boots. He's a
self-made man. He's not an aristocrat.

01:50:16.444 --> 01:50:23.965 align:start position:0%
The country should be run by people of
noble blood, the true counselors of the

01:50:20.005 --> 01:50:23.965 align:start position:0%
king, not these sort of upstarts.

01:50:24.165 --> 01:50:31.125 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; To remove Cromwell from power, Norfolk
starts a campaign aimed at discrediting

01:50:28.805 --> 01:50:31.125 align:start position:0%
him.

01:50:31.165 --> 01:50:37.045 align:start position:0%
It doesn't take much [music] to stoke
Henry's suspicions.

01:50:35.525 --> 01:50:41.525 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Norfolk claimed that Cromwell was
plotting to marry the king's daughter

01:50:38.805 --> 01:50:46.485 align:start position:0%
Mary, make himself king. He pointed out
the fact he had this huge household that

01:50:44.445 --> 01:50:51.045 align:start position:0%
could perhaps turn into a private army
and take the throne by force. There was

01:50:48.805 --> 01:50:57.125 align:start position:0%
literally no evidence behind any of the
charges, but Norfolk knew Henry was so

01:50:54.285 --> 01:51:02.005 align:start position:0%
paranoid that he would believe it.
&gt;&gt; Henry was thinking if Cromwell has let

01:50:59.165 --> 01:51:05.285 align:start position:0%
him down, he must have meant it. He must
have been in some way acting cruelly to

01:51:03.645 --> 01:51:08.645 align:start position:0%
the king, and Henry's ego was
particularly precious and particularly

01:51:07.125 --> 01:51:11.325 align:start position:0%
vulnerable where he thought he'd been
betrayed.

01:51:14.125 --> 01:51:20.645 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; For Cromwell,
it's only a matter of time before Henry

01:51:17.805 --> 01:51:20.645 align:start position:0%
turns on him.

01:51:26.885 --> 01:51:33.325 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Thomas Cromwell knew the end was coming.
He could smell it.

01:51:31.765 --> 01:51:38.245 align:start position:0%
He must have constantly been looking
over his shoulder, not knowing who to

01:51:35.645 --> 01:51:38.245 align:start position:0%
trust.

01:51:39.525 --> 01:51:44.085 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry finally gives the order to strike.

01:51:45.805 --> 01:51:51.165 align:start position:0%
And when Cromwell arrives late at a
privy council meeting,

01:51:51.885 --> 01:51:59.685 align:start position:0%
the Duke of Norfolk is waiting for him.
&gt;&gt; We don't know why he was late. It might

01:51:57.205 --> 01:52:03.405 align:start position:0%
have all been part of the plot, but he's
thought it was just a routine meeting.

01:52:01.845 --> 01:52:08.405 align:start position:0%
And this is a man who has this
sophisticated spy network. He knows

01:52:05.285 --> 01:52:13.245 align:start position:0%
everything. He didn't know this.
&gt;&gt; When he moves to sit down, Norfolk said,

01:52:11.125 --> 01:52:17.805 align:start position:0%
"Stop. That's not the seat for a
traitor."

01:52:15.005 --> 01:52:23.246 align:start position:0%
Cromwell was frozen.
&gt;&gt; He must have been absolutely terrified

01:52:19.726 --> 01:52:23.246 align:start position:0%
cuz he knows where it ends.

01:52:25.726 --> 01:52:32.326 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; When the guards rushed forward, there
was a cry of traitor and he was seized.

01:52:32.566 --> 01:52:38.646 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He was astonished and he said, "Well,
why are you calling me a traitor? Tell

01:52:35.606 --> 01:52:43.766 align:start position:0%
me what the charges are."
&gt;&gt; Nobody said a word because they hadn't

01:52:41.046 --> 01:52:46.766 align:start position:0%
finished making those charges up yet.
They had no answer.

01:52:45.366 --> 01:52:51.246 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; There's a moment that's almost
Shakespearean where the Duke of Norfolk

01:52:49.126 --> 01:52:55.966 align:start position:0%
rips the chain of office from around his
neck.

01:52:53.006 --> 01:53:02.086 align:start position:0%
This method of arrest has been devised
deliberately to surprise and shock him.

01:52:59.006 --> 01:53:06.646 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He was dragged out and taken by boat to
the Tower of London on that dreadful

01:53:03.766 --> 01:53:06.646 align:start position:0%
one-way ticket.

01:53:18.206 --> 01:53:23.406 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry VIII has [music] been on the
throne for over three decades.

01:53:25.766 --> 01:53:34.086 align:start position:0%
After ordering the arrest of his chief
[music] minister, Thomas Cromwell,

01:53:30.046 --> 01:53:34.086 align:start position:0%
Henry's suspicions intensify.

01:53:34.406 --> 01:53:40.726 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; After Cromwell's fall, Henry is actually
a rather different character [music]

01:53:38.126 --> 01:53:44.606 align:start position:0%
because he starts to say for the first
time, "I trust no one but myself."

01:53:43.326 --> 01:53:47.486 align:start position:0%
He doesn't appoint another chief
minister.

01:53:45.926 --> 01:53:51.326 align:start position:0%
And, you know, people have said, "Oh,
these are years without a policy, you

01:53:49.326 --> 01:53:56.406 align:start position:0%
know, no one was up to the job." No, no,
no, no, no, no. Henry believed he was up

01:53:54.006 --> 01:53:59.886 align:start position:0%
to the job. He was going to direct
everything.

01:53:57.446 --> 01:54:02.886 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He was so sensitive to any accusation
that he was being governed by other

01:54:01.286 --> 01:54:06.966 align:start position:0%
people, that other people were
manipulating him, that he was the

01:54:04.446 --> 01:54:10.646 align:start position:0%
plaything of other people's ambitions,
that he did everything in his power to

01:54:08.646 --> 01:54:15.526 align:start position:0%
try and assert himself as the ultimate
authority in the kingdom.

01:54:13.446 --> 01:54:18.886 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Even though Cromwell is now his prisoner
in the Tower,

01:54:16.846 --> 01:54:21.366 align:start position:0%
Henry still needs his former advisor's
help.

01:54:22.006 --> 01:54:28.048 align:start position:0%
Henry remains trapped in his to Anne of
Cleves,

01:54:25.568 --> 01:54:32.488 align:start position:0%
and he needs Cromwell's legal expertise
to get him out of it.

01:54:30.688 --> 01:54:36.808 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; There's nobody else who can get him out
of this fiasco marriage with Anne of

01:54:35.008 --> 01:54:40.887 align:start position:0%
Cleves. So, Henry's writing to Cromwell
asking for his help. You know, give me

01:54:38.568 --> 01:54:47.488 align:start position:0%
evidence that [music] the marriage was
never valid, that it could be annulled.

01:54:43.768 --> 01:54:50.768 align:start position:0%
So, Cromwell is working for Henry till
his very last breath.

01:54:52.608 --> 01:54:58.288 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; I think that he believes that the king
at some point is going to turn around

01:54:57.048 --> 01:55:01.168 align:start position:0%
and say,
"Sorry, all is forgiven. This is a

01:54:59.887 --> 01:55:04.648 align:start position:0%
mistake.
I'm going to release you. Live out the

01:55:02.728 --> 01:55:10.488 align:start position:0%
rest of your years. Um we're going to
find a place for you somewhere."

01:55:08.728 --> 01:55:13.927 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But once the Anne of Cleves marriage is
annulled,

01:55:11.887 --> 01:55:16.568 align:start position:0%
Henry has no further use for his former
adviser.

01:55:19.528 --> 01:55:25.528 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Someone like Thomas Cromwell is
&gt;&gt; a friend. He's a human tool of whatever

01:55:23.568 --> 01:55:29.568 align:start position:0%
it is that Henry wished to achieve at
any moment. And so, he will pick a tool

01:55:27.688 --> 01:55:33.648 align:start position:0%
up and he will use it. And when it no
longer serves its purpose, he'll cast it

01:55:31.488 --> 01:55:38.688 align:start position:0%
aside.
&gt;&gt; On the 28th of July, 1540,

01:55:36.488 --> 01:55:42.847 align:start position:0%
Thomas Cromwell, once one of the most
powerful men in England, [music]

01:55:40.648 --> 01:55:46.648 align:start position:0%
is led to the scaffold and publicly
executed on Tower Hill.

01:55:50.168 --> 01:55:56.768 align:start position:0%
With Cromwell out of the way,
his arch enemy, the Duke of Norfolk,

01:55:54.648 --> 01:56:02.248 align:start position:0%
sees an opportunity to secure greater
powers for himself.

01:55:59.568 --> 01:56:07.168 align:start position:0%
And he has a secret weapon to help him,
his teenage niece,

01:56:04.208 --> 01:56:07.168 align:start position:0%
Catherine Howard.

01:56:08.367 --> 01:56:13.568 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The moment that Catherine Howard was in
the king's bed, Norfolk probably thought

01:56:11.448 --> 01:56:17.887 align:start position:0%
he was absolutely made for life.
&gt;&gt; I mean, Norfolk was a cynical,

01:56:15.048 --> 01:56:21.847 align:start position:0%
unpleasant career aristocrat who beat
his wife, knocked her teeth out. I mean,

01:56:19.927 --> 01:56:25.609 align:start position:0%
this was not a nice man.
So, the fact that he was using women as

01:56:23.407 --> 01:56:29.289 align:start position:0%
pawns in a political game shouldn't
surprise us.

01:56:26.689 --> 01:56:29.289 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He liked it here.

01:56:29.649 --> 01:56:36.569 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Norfolk's position [music] is secured
when Henry takes Catherine Howard as his

01:56:34.329 --> 01:56:43.129 align:start position:0%
fifth wife.
&gt;&gt; He seems to rediscover something of his

01:56:38.969 --> 01:56:48.729 align:start position:0%
lost youth in her. He adores her and is
seen playing with her in public. So, he

01:56:46.729 --> 01:56:53.009 align:start position:0%
feels himself to be this young king
again.

01:56:50.809 --> 01:56:58.529 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He wanted to prove to everyone around
him that he was a virile man and I think

01:56:56.369 --> 01:57:03.009 align:start position:0%
that his caressing of Catherine Howard,
his constant parading her about this

01:57:00.569 --> 01:57:08.209 align:start position:0%
place as this young bride on his arm is
just massive overcompensation.

01:57:05.289 --> 01:57:12.049 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He's old enough to be a grandfather, so
they must have presented this rather

01:57:10.249 --> 01:57:14.609 align:start position:0%
incongruous image of Beauty and the
Beast.

01:57:21.369 --> 01:57:28.409 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But Henry and [music] Catherine's
honeymoon is short-lived.

01:57:25.809 --> 01:57:34.289 align:start position:0%
After just 15 months together,
evidence emerges that Catherine wasn't a

01:57:30.849 --> 01:57:34.289 align:start position:0%
virgin when she married him.

01:57:34.369 --> 01:57:42.209 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; On the 2nd of November, 1541, Henry VIII
was at mass up in the King's Closet just

01:57:40.329 --> 01:57:46.089 align:start position:0%
above us here in the Chapel Royal of
Hampton Court Palace and he was

01:57:44.009 --> 01:57:51.369 align:start position:0%
presented with a letter from Archbishop
Cranmer that relayed the sordid details

01:57:49.009 --> 01:57:55.649 align:start position:0%
of Catherine Howard's past and it
explicitly says in this account that

01:57:53.409 --> 01:57:59.609 align:start position:0%
Cranmer didn't just tell the king this
information, but instead put it in

01:57:57.569 --> 01:58:03.769 align:start position:0%
writing. He declared the information
thereof to his highness

01:58:01.928 --> 01:58:08.129 align:start position:0%
in writing.
Because as it says here, he had not the

01:58:05.489 --> 01:58:11.649 align:start position:0%
heart to express the same to the king by
word of mouth and I can easily imagine

01:58:10.329 --> 01:58:15.609 align:start position:0%
that he wouldn't have the heart to tell
the king that his jewel of womanhood was

01:58:13.849 --> 01:58:19.448 align:start position:0%
in fact a woman of considerable sexual
experience.

01:58:17.569 --> 01:58:23.849 align:start position:0%
This account makes it very clear that
Henry was completely heartbroken when he

01:58:22.049 --> 01:58:28.330 align:start position:0%
discovered this news. It says his joy
was turned to sorrow. He wept bitter

01:58:26.169 --> 01:58:33.010 align:start position:0%
tears and you get this impression of
someone who really, really wanted this

01:58:30.530 --> 01:58:37.810 align:start position:0%
marriage to work, who was deeply in love
with Catherine Howard, and whose world

01:58:34.970 --> 01:58:41.330 align:start position:0%
just came crumbling down around him when
he found out the truth about her.

01:58:43.410 --> 01:58:50.170 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Several days later, the allegations
against Catherine intensify. [music]

01:58:48.410 --> 01:58:53.690 align:start position:0%
And she is accused of having an affair
during her marriage to Henry.

01:58:53.850 --> 01:58:59.130 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The moment he learned about this, the
moment he learned that it was true that

01:58:56.730 --> 01:59:03.610 align:start position:0%
she had had an affair, he left. And
that's what we see Henry doing time and

01:59:00.930 --> 01:59:07.650 align:start position:0%
time again in his relationships. It's
quite disturbing that Henry has this

01:59:05.410 --> 01:59:14.690 align:start position:0%
capacity to just [music] sort of turn
off and move on from a person, even one

01:59:11.050 --> 01:59:19.770 align:start position:0%
who clearly he loved very deeply.
&gt;&gt; Catherine Howard's fate is clear the

01:59:17.090 --> 01:59:24.410 align:start position:0%
moment Henry turns against her.
She is beheaded for treason at the Tower

01:59:21.810 --> 01:59:24.410 align:start position:0%
of [music] London.

01:59:24.810 --> 01:59:32.330 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Catherine was just a girl who'd been
taken advantage of by men for most of

01:59:29.530 --> 01:59:36.317 align:start position:0%
her life, who ended up dying very
bravely,

01:59:33.650 --> 01:59:36.317 align:start position:0%
but very horribly. [music]

01:59:36.370 --> 01:59:46.210 align:start position:0%
After Catherine Howard, Henry's left
with the reality of an aging man who's

01:59:42.730 --> 01:59:51.450 align:start position:0%
losing his virility. There is a sense of
deep unhappiness that this is what he

01:59:49.490 --> 01:59:55.170 align:start position:0%
now has to live with, this
the wreck of the prince he once was.

01:59:56.370 --> 02:00:05.890 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Despite five failed marriages, Henry
only has one legitimate son.

02:00:02.810 --> 02:00:09.250 align:start position:0%
So, he embarks on his sixth marriage
to Catherine Parr,

02:00:07.570 --> 02:00:12.290 align:start position:0%
hopeful that she will provide him with a
spare heir.

02:00:13.450 --> 02:00:20.170 align:start position:0%
But Henry's also increasingly [music]
concerned about his imperial legacy.

02:00:18.130 --> 02:00:23.730 align:start position:0%
And for a Tudor king, that means only
one thing,

02:00:21.570 --> 02:00:28.690 align:start position:0%
going to war.
&gt;&gt; He's trying to recapture his lost youth,

02:00:26.290 --> 02:00:32.812 align:start position:0%
and he tries to do that by going off to
war. He's going to be this great

02:00:30.212 --> 02:00:38.492 align:start position:0%
crusading king again, reclaiming parts
of France.

02:00:34.092 --> 02:00:42.052 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry grew up on tales of daring do
against the French.

02:00:40.412 --> 02:00:46.772 align:start position:0%
Henry V,
Agincourt,

02:00:43.612 --> 02:00:49.932 align:start position:0%
and all those other famous victories.
&gt;&gt; Henry had always wanted to have military

02:00:48.372 --> 02:00:53.812 align:start position:0%
glory in [music] his portfolio of
achievements. In this period, the

02:00:52.172 --> 02:00:57.172 align:start position:0%
English nobility want to go smashing up
the French and just like [music] 21st

02:00:55.452 --> 02:01:01.092 align:start position:0%
century tourists want to go, you know,
around northern France on holiday.

02:01:01.413 --> 02:01:06.692 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; Here at Windsor Castle is a treasure

02:01:04.972 --> 02:01:10.932 align:start position:0%
that epitomizes Henry's image of [music]
himself as a warrior king.

02:01:11.652 --> 02:01:18.212 align:start position:0%
In the latter years of his reign, Henry
specially commissions this suit of

02:01:16.052 --> 02:01:24.412 align:start position:0%
armor.
&gt;&gt; Here is the physical embodiment of

02:01:20.532 --> 02:01:31.252 align:start position:0%
Henry's childhood dreams, the symbol of
chivalry and the image of an armored

02:01:27.532 --> 02:01:35.452 align:start position:0%
man, Henry VIII's armor.
Now, armor in the 16th century was made

02:01:33.772 --> 02:01:40.092 align:start position:0%
to measure, none of this off-the-peg
stuff. It provides us with the true

02:01:37.772 --> 02:01:46.052 align:start position:0%
image of Henry as he would like to be
projected, of power and might and

02:01:43.572 --> 02:01:51.849 align:start position:0%
ruthlessness. You can almost imagine his
little piggy eyes behind that visor

02:01:49.492 --> 02:01:53.869 align:start position:0%
glaring at us with contempt.
&gt;&gt; [music]

02:01:55.492 --> 02:02:01.532 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Despite the commanding image that Henry
wants to project,

02:01:59.452 --> 02:02:05.532 align:start position:0%
his armor is actually enlarged to
accommodate his increasing size.

02:02:05.612 --> 02:02:12.532 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Here, they're having to let in 5 cm
plates on each side of his back plate

02:02:09.892 --> 02:02:18.892 align:start position:0%
because of his expanding girth, cuz he
did weigh 28 stone.

02:02:15.092 --> 02:02:28.529 align:start position:0%
Now, in National Health Service terms,
his body mass index was way off today's

02:02:22.572 --> 02:02:30.549 align:start position:0%
scale. He was a man mountain.
&gt;&gt; [music]

02:02:31.892 --> 02:02:38.853 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; In order to make him feel more
comfortable and to flatter him, his male

02:02:36.253 --> 02:02:44.013 align:start position:0%
courtiers start to wear [music] enormous
padded doublets and clothes so that they

02:02:41.533 --> 02:02:49.413 align:start position:0%
appear just as big as the king. This
also affected Henry's psyche. I think he

02:02:47.093 --> 02:02:53.333 align:start position:0%
was really humiliated by what he had
become. [music]

02:02:51.133 --> 02:02:59.533 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's very aware that his advancing
years and medical disorders threaten to

02:02:55.973 --> 02:03:04.773 align:start position:0%
derail his battlefield ambitions.
So, while he still can, he personally

02:03:02.213 --> 02:03:08.333 align:start position:0%
launches an assault on the French port
of Boulogne.

02:03:06.773 --> 02:03:11.973 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; I mean, his idea of leading his army in
person, of course, means directing

02:03:09.773 --> 02:03:17.133 align:start position:0%
operations from a safe distance inside a
um a sort of wooden pavilion, which is

02:03:14.133 --> 02:03:22.240 align:start position:0%
lined [music] with fake marble inside.
&gt;&gt; He is like a small boy

02:03:19.973 --> 02:03:25.013 align:start position:0%
with lots of toy soldiers.
&gt;&gt; [music]

02:03:22.493 --> 02:03:28.693 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; He is in his element.
He loves

02:03:26.653 --> 02:03:33.253 align:start position:0%
the siege. He loves
all these cannonades, which fire day and

02:03:31.253 --> 02:03:37.173 align:start position:0%
night.
&gt;&gt; It was an attempt to gain glory by

02:03:35.253 --> 02:03:41.773 align:start position:0%
conquering France again. It was an
attempt to resurrect the idea that

02:03:39.413 --> 02:03:45.820 align:start position:0%
England would be mighty by ruling over
France.

02:03:43.733 --> 02:03:48.893 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's attack on Boulogne is a success.
[music]

02:03:46.893 --> 02:03:53.893 align:start position:0%
And he enters the captured port as a
conquering hero.

02:03:51.253 --> 02:03:58.293 align:start position:0%
But his vanity project has a serious
impact on England's economy.

02:03:59.013 --> 02:04:07.373 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry painted the capture of Boulogne as
a great victory, but it cost them

02:04:03.733 --> 02:04:11.493 align:start position:0%
enormous sums of money. And in fact,
England became bankrupt by the cost of

02:04:09.893 --> 02:04:16.373 align:start position:0%
war.
&gt;&gt; Five years after Henry died, a Tudor

02:04:13.973 --> 02:04:22.453 align:start position:0%
accountant was given the task of
calculating how much the wars had cost.

02:04:20.173 --> 02:04:26.493 align:start position:0%
He produced a 16-page
account,

02:04:23.773 --> 02:04:31.573 align:start position:0%
which showed that it had cost the poor
English taxpayer equivalent in today's

02:04:29.013 --> 02:04:37.255 align:start position:0%
money 1.87
billion pounds. And

02:04:34.653 --> 02:04:43.454 align:start position:0%
it shows the burden which his subjects
had to bear to pay for his hopes and

02:04:40.494 --> 02:04:43.454 align:start position:0%
military glory.

02:04:44.574 --> 02:04:49.974 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Despite plunging England into
bankruptcy,

02:04:47.454 --> 02:04:52.735 align:start position:0%
Henry's military ambitions do have some
benefits.

02:04:53.094 --> 02:04:59.175 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's military legacy was enormously
positive. Yes, he'd depleted the royal

02:04:57.454 --> 02:05:04.735 align:start position:0%
treasury in the process, but he'd
created one of the greatest navies in

02:05:02.135 --> 02:05:10.175 align:start position:0%
the world and also an incredibly
impressive army as well. He'd made

02:05:06.894 --> 02:05:13.695 align:start position:0%
England a power to be reckoned with.
&gt;&gt; I think Henry understood that all

02:05:11.894 --> 02:05:19.255 align:start position:0%
nations in the early modern period were
unstable, and so you had to maintain the

02:05:16.934 --> 02:05:23.334 align:start position:0%
appearance of a strong king able to
deliver justice, able to lead the nation

02:05:21.454 --> 02:05:26.494 align:start position:0%
in war. These were the things that
united the realm.

02:05:24.974 --> 02:05:31.374 align:start position:0%
Henry would have been seen as a good
king because of a king who leads to

02:05:28.815 --> 02:05:34.655 align:start position:0%
victory in a war is a good king almost
regardless of anything else.

02:05:36.414 --> 02:05:41.255 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But just after Henry secures the
military legacy he's always [music]

02:05:39.934 --> 02:05:45.735 align:start position:0%
dreamed of,
his health takes a turn for the worse.

02:05:56.655 --> 02:06:03.574 align:start position:0%
As his health deteriorates, Henry takes
to shutting himself away in his

02:06:00.934 --> 02:06:03.574 align:start position:0%
chambers.

02:06:05.735 --> 02:06:09.014 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The last years of the reign are
definitely changed [music] by

02:06:07.614 --> 02:06:11.735 align:start position:0%
claustrophobia.
You know, no one quite knows who to

02:06:10.215 --> 02:06:16.135 align:start position:0%
trust. And of course, because of his
immobility, Henry is closeted in a

02:06:14.414 --> 02:06:19.374 align:start position:0%
secret [music] study at the far end of
Whitehall Palace and doesn't come out

02:06:18.054 --> 02:06:22.815 align:start position:0%
that much.
People think that, okay, he's sort of

02:06:21.175 --> 02:06:26.894 align:start position:0%
switched off. This is not the case. I
mean, this is somebody who is almost

02:06:24.655 --> 02:06:33.014 align:start position:0%
like uh in his lair, he's checking up on
everything.

02:06:29.094 --> 02:06:38.416 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; A good way to view Henry would be as a
rather malignant spider at the center of

02:06:36.054 --> 02:06:43.416 align:start position:0%
everything which went on within England.
all those lines of the web, all run

02:06:42.135 --> 02:06:46.816 align:start position:0%
through
and end up with him.

02:06:48.216 --> 02:06:55.935 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; It's becoming clear to Henry's courtiers
that he's nearing the end.

02:06:53.856 --> 02:07:00.357 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; In the last days of Henry's life, the
atmosphere at court must have been

02:06:57.495 --> 02:07:04.696 align:start position:0%
pretty toxic. There was a sense of fear,
[music] of anxiety, of uncertainty for

02:07:02.935 --> 02:07:09.656 align:start position:0%
what the future would hold. There was a
real sense, I think, that the end was

02:07:06.776 --> 02:07:13.816 align:start position:0%
coming for King Henry VIII.
&gt;&gt; But no one [music] is brave enough to

02:07:11.176 --> 02:07:19.455 align:start position:0%
mention this to Henry himself.
&gt;&gt; A dying king is like a dying lion,

02:07:16.216 --> 02:07:24.256 align:start position:0%
extraordinarily dangerous.
&gt;&gt; Everybody was terrified that Henry still

02:07:21.816 --> 02:07:27.095 align:start position:0%
had the power to kill. It was said that
no one would give him any official

02:07:25.896 --> 02:07:30.975 align:start position:0%
advice
because they were frightened of his

02:07:28.256 --> 02:07:30.975 align:start position:0%
reaction.

02:07:31.135 --> 02:07:36.336 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Imagining the death of the king was
treason. So, in a capricious reign,

02:07:34.935 --> 02:07:40.376 align:start position:0%
where people had been charged with
treason for all kinds of offenses,

02:07:38.416 --> 02:07:45.015 align:start position:0%
simply telling the king that he might
die is not something that even the

02:07:42.336 --> 02:07:48.376 align:start position:0%
bravest counselors would be able to do.
The only thing to say to a king is,

02:07:47.055 --> 02:07:53.296 align:start position:0%
"It's a scratch. You're sure to get
better. Tomorrow we'll go hunting.

02:07:50.176 --> 02:07:53.296 align:start position:0%
Everything will be fine."

02:07:53.935 --> 02:08:02.176 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; As Henry's health gets worse, the
finishing touches are put on one of the

02:07:57.975 --> 02:08:02.176 align:start position:0%
most important documents of his reign.

02:08:02.615 --> 02:08:10.216 align:start position:0%
His last will and testament.
It reveals his attempts to retain

02:08:07.975 --> 02:08:13.615 align:start position:0%
control over his kingdom
even after his death.

02:08:14.176 --> 02:08:23.336 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; This, very excitingly, is the last will
and testament of King Henry VIII.

02:08:20.535 --> 02:08:28.095 align:start position:0%
Here you see Henry R, Henry Rex, Henry
the King.

02:08:24.935 --> 02:08:32.455 align:start position:0%
This is Henry's last-ditch attempt at
controlling the future of England.

02:08:30.975 --> 02:08:38.376 align:start position:0%
If you ever needed proof that Henry was
a bit of a megalomaniac, this is it.

02:08:36.376 --> 02:08:42.577 align:start position:0%
An enormous proportion of this will is
taken up with the thing that had

02:08:39.455 --> 02:08:47.177 align:start position:0%
concerned Henry right from the moment he
acceded to the throne, which is the

02:08:44.417 --> 02:08:51.817 align:start position:0%
succession to the dynasty of the Tudors
after Henry died. It's not a surprise

02:08:49.817 --> 02:08:56.897 align:start position:0%
that of course what Henry most wants is
his son Edward to become king after him.

02:08:54.897 --> 02:09:01.977 align:start position:0%
But, perhaps because he himself was a
second son, he provides for the

02:08:58.857 --> 02:09:07.297 align:start position:0%
possibility that Edward might die.
In other words, even on his deathbed,

02:09:04.457 --> 02:09:12.657 align:start position:0%
Henry is still trying to claw his way
into control beyond the grave. Even more

02:09:10.777 --> 02:09:17.497 align:start position:0%
extraordinarily, given that Henry, as I
say, is dying at this point, he provides

02:09:15.497 --> 02:09:23.657 align:start position:0%
for the possibility that there might
even be another wife in his future.

02:09:20.697 --> 02:09:27.537 align:start position:0%
Any lawful wife who I shall hereafter
marry.

02:09:25.737 --> 02:09:31.897 align:start position:0%
I mean, that is rank optimism in the
face of

02:09:28.777 --> 02:09:37.617 align:start position:0%
all possible evidence, I would say.
I think there's something almost tragic

02:09:34.497 --> 02:09:42.777 align:start position:0%
about this king on his deathbed who has
striven for nearly 40 years to have

02:09:40.257 --> 02:09:46.457 align:start position:0%
absolute power over the people in his
country.

02:09:43.857 --> 02:09:51.697 align:start position:0%
And now in his dying moments, he's still
trying to do that. He's still trying to

02:09:49.017 --> 02:09:58.137 align:start position:0%
maintain control. And there's something
moving about that, almost admirable,

02:09:55.537 --> 02:10:01.217 align:start position:0%
uh and also slightly repulsive, if I'm
completely honest.

02:10:04.697 --> 02:10:11.337 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry is growing so ill that he's
started to drift in and out of

02:10:08.537 --> 02:10:11.337 align:start position:0%
consciousness.

02:10:12.297 --> 02:10:17.457 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; When Henry was on his deathbed, he must
have felt that his dynasty was coming to

02:10:16.017 --> 02:10:23.137 align:start position:0%
an end.
Henry wasn't in a position to pass on

02:10:20.057 --> 02:10:29.057 align:start position:0%
his crown to another stable male
monarch.

02:10:24.737 --> 02:10:32.537 align:start position:0%
His son, Edward, was still very young.
&gt;&gt; When Henry knows that he really is

02:10:30.614 --> 02:10:36.137 align:start position:0%
[music] now going to die, he must have
been wondering if he was going to end up

02:10:34.257 --> 02:10:41.177 align:start position:0%
on the right side of things with God. I
mean, he was Christ's deputy on Earth,

02:10:38.737 --> 02:10:46.459 align:start position:0%
but he was also going to be judged. And
Henry must have been wondering whether

02:10:42.939 --> 02:10:51.739 align:start position:0%
actually he had quite got things right.
&gt;&gt; Henry was now presiding over a realm

02:10:48.459 --> 02:10:56.899 align:start position:0%
divided in which religion had become an
irreconcilable grievance.

02:10:54.138 --> 02:11:00.939 align:start position:0%
Henry's lifetime as king had seen the
creation of a divided England.

02:10:59.459 --> 02:11:03.779 align:start position:0%
And that was a genie he couldn't put
back in the bottle.

02:11:05.419 --> 02:11:11.539 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry's courtiers finally mustered the
courage to warn him of his approaching

02:11:10.138 --> 02:11:17.178 align:start position:0%
death.
&gt;&gt; There was a great deal of tension in the

02:11:13.459 --> 02:11:21.619 align:start position:0%
court. Who was going to tell the king
that he was about to meet his maker?

02:11:19.939 --> 02:11:27.339 align:start position:0%
Eventually,
the task fell to Sir Anthony Denny, who

02:11:24.579 --> 02:11:32.979 align:start position:0%
in life had fulfilled Henry's most
intimate needs as groom of the stool.

02:11:29.779 --> 02:11:38.059 align:start position:0%
Now, he had one last service to perform
for his master, to tell him he was

02:11:35.579 --> 02:11:42.459 align:start position:0%
dying.
&gt;&gt; He asked Henry effectively if he wanted

02:11:40.619 --> 02:11:45.941 align:start position:0%
to make his last confession. Should I
send for Thomas Cranmer, the Archbishop

02:11:44.899 --> 02:11:49.379 align:start position:0%
of Canterbury?
&gt;&gt; [music]

02:11:46.138 --> 02:11:55.939 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; And Henry replied and said, "I will
first take a little sleep.

02:11:52.178 --> 02:11:59.579 align:start position:0%
And then, as I feel myself,
I will think on the matter."

02:12:00.539 --> 02:12:04.859 align:start position:0%
They were the last words he ever spoke.

02:12:07.178 --> 02:12:14.739 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; On the 28th of January, 1547,
Henry VIII

02:12:12.099 --> 02:12:14.739 align:start position:0%
dies.

02:12:15.219 --> 02:12:22.219 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry VIII has gone down in history as
our most famous king. Probably because

02:12:19.739 --> 02:12:27.779 align:start position:0%
he's our most married king. He's a kind
of larger-than-life character. But, it's

02:12:25.259 --> 02:12:34.619 align:start position:0%
very, very clear that behind this public
facade was somebody who was

02:12:30.219 --> 02:12:40.059 align:start position:0%
fundamentally vulnerable and insecure.
&gt;&gt; The story of Henry VIII has [music]

02:12:36.459 --> 02:12:45.860 align:start position:0%
everything in it. It has transition from
young, irresponsible being to someone

02:12:42.939 --> 02:12:50.900 align:start position:0%
blighted later in life by paranoia.
&gt;&gt; Henry was self-obsessed, desired

02:12:48.420 --> 02:12:56.580 align:start position:0%
admiration. He could never be wrong. You
cannot ignore Henry.

02:12:54.180 --> 02:13:01.660 align:start position:0%
He put England in the center of European
politics.

02:12:58.180 --> 02:13:04.820 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But he also gave the English a sense of
national identity. [music]

02:13:03.540 --> 02:13:08.420 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; England was never going to be quite the
same after Henry.

02:13:06.500 --> 02:13:12.940 align:start position:0%
He'd broken with Rome. He [music] had
centralized the kingdom. Institutions

02:13:10.739 --> 02:13:18.297 align:start position:0%
like Parliament, the Church of England
hardly changed for another 400 years.

02:13:16.420 --> 02:13:21.660 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Henry was tremendously charismatic.
[music]

02:13:18.900 --> 02:13:26.060 align:start position:0%
He knew how to be a king. He understood
the myth of English kingship.

02:13:24.700 --> 02:13:29.980 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; I think if you looked at Henry VIII's
reign as a whole,

02:13:27.780 --> 02:13:35.580 align:start position:0%
you would have to accept that it had
been a reign that changed the state of

02:13:32.420 --> 02:13:35.580 align:start position:0%
England forever.

02:13:53.667 --> 02:13:55.687 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]

